1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:03,340
You're tired — I know.

2
00:00:04,220 --> 00:00:09,240
This isn't something you have to listen
to, it's just something to fall asleep in.

3
00:00:10,160 --> 00:00:15,700
The whole Gospel of Luke, read slowly, and
then Ecclesiastes.

4
00:00:16,260 --> 00:00:17,300
Close your eyes.

5
00:00:17,800 --> 00:00:21,660
If you'd like something carried in prayer
tonight, leave it in the comments.

6
00:00:22,560 --> 00:00:24,900
Subscribe if these readings help you
sleep.

7
00:00:25,900 --> 00:00:29,460
Lord, you know how long this stretch has
been.

8
00:00:30,260 --> 00:00:36,300
Not one bad day — a run of
them, close enough together that I've stopped counting.

9
00:00:37,420 --> 00:00:42,680
I keep waiting for the week that
finally feels different, and it keeps not arriving.

10
00:00:43,540 --> 00:00:46,200
I'm not asking you to explain the season
I'm in.

11
00:00:47,540 --> 00:00:53,300
Ecclesiastes says there is a time for
everything, and I believe it, though I'd rather

12
00:00:53,340 --> 00:00:56,880
be past this particular time than in the
middle of it.

13
00:00:57,940 --> 00:01:00,900
What I need tonight is smaller than an
answer.

14
00:01:01,900 --> 00:01:03,940
I need to stop straining for a while.

15
00:01:04,420 --> 00:01:11,000
So let Luke's account of your Son go past
me slowly — the long walk of it, the

16
00:01:11,040 --> 00:01:13,700
meals, the people he stopped for.

17
00:01:14,500 --> 00:01:15,700
He was never in a hurry.

18
00:01:16,640 --> 00:01:18,080
Let some of that reach me.

19
00:01:18,920 --> 00:01:20,560
Take the ache out of my shoulders.

20
00:01:21,400 --> 00:01:23,180
Take the argument out of my head.

21
00:01:23,220 --> 00:01:29,020
Let me sleep the way a child sleeps in
a house where someone else is awake and keeping

22
00:01:29,060 --> 00:01:29,960
watch.

23
00:01:30,600 --> 00:01:35,880
And be gentle tonight with everyone else
who has run out of ways to fix things.

24
00:01:36,840 --> 00:01:37,740
Amen.

25
00:01:38,240 --> 00:01:40,500
Luke, chapter one.

26
00:01:40,540 --> 00:01:45,640
Since many have undertaken to set in order
a narrative concerning those matters which

27
00:01:45,680 --> 00:01:51,660
have been fulfilled amongst us, even as
those who from the beginning were eyewitnesses

28
00:01:51,700 --> 00:01:58,060
and servants of the word delivered them to
us, it seemed good to me also, having traced

29
00:01:58,100 --> 00:02:05,000
the course of all things accurately from the
first, to write to you in order, most excellent

30
00:02:05,040 --> 00:02:10,380
Theophilus; that you might know the certainty
concerning the things in which you were

31
00:02:10,420 --> 00:02:11,320
instructed.

32
00:02:11,600 --> 00:02:17,720
There was in the days of Herod, the
king of Judea, a certain priest named Zacharias,

33
00:02:17,760 --> 00:02:20,540
of the priestly division of Abijah.

34
00:02:21,600 --> 00:02:25,520
He had a wife of the daughters of Aaron,
and her name was Elizabeth.

35
00:02:26,097 --> 00:02:32,117
They were both righteous before God,
walking blamelessly in all the commandments and

36
00:02:32,157 --> 00:02:33,557
ordinances of the Lord.

37
00:02:34,297 --> 00:02:40,837
But they had no child, because Elizabeth
was barren, and they both were well advanced

38
00:02:40,877 --> 00:02:41,777
in years.

39
00:02:42,037 --> 00:02:47,737
Now while he executed the priest’s office before
God in the order of his division according

40
00:02:47,777 --> 00:02:53,837
to the custom of the priest’s office, his lot
was to enter into the temple of the Lord

41
00:02:53,877 --> 00:02:55,377
and burn incense.

42
00:02:56,417 --> 00:03:01,037
The whole multitude of the people were
praying outside at the hour of incense.

43
00:03:01,657 --> 00:03:07,137
An angel of the Lord appeared to him, standing
on the right side of the altar of incense.

44
00:03:08,437 --> 00:03:12,757
Zacharias was troubled when he saw him,
and fear fell upon him.

45
00:03:13,577 --> 00:03:19,677
But the angel said to him, “Don’t
be afraid, Zacharias, because your request has been

46
00:03:19,717 --> 00:03:20,617
heard.

47
00:03:20,777 --> 00:03:25,737
Your wife, Elizabeth, will bear you a son,
and you shall call his name John.

48
00:03:26,857 --> 00:03:31,437
You will have joy and gladness, and many
will rejoice at his birth.

49
00:03:32,317 --> 00:03:38,217
For he will be great in the sight of the
Lord, and he will drink no wine nor strong drink.

50
00:03:38,797 --> 00:03:43,237
He will be filled with the Holy Spirit,
even from his mother’s womb.

51
00:03:44,197 --> 00:03:48,257
He will turn many of the children of
Israel to the Lord their God.

52
00:03:48,797 --> 00:03:54,477
He will go before him in the spirit and
power of Elijah, ‘to turn the hearts of the fathers

53
00:03:54,517 --> 00:04:00,717
to the children,’ and the disobedient to the
wisdom of the just; to prepare a people

54
00:04:00,757 --> 00:04:02,157
prepared for the Lord.”

55
00:04:03,877 --> 00:04:07,617
Zacharias said to the angel, “How can I be
sure of this?

56
00:04:08,537 --> 00:04:12,937
For I am an old man, and my wife is well
advanced in years.”

57
00:04:13,897 --> 00:04:20,017
The angel answered him, “I am Gabriel, who
stands in the presence of God.

58
00:04:20,717 --> 00:04:24,217
I was sent to speak to you and to bring
you this good news.

59
00:04:25,197 --> 00:04:31,237
Behold, you will be silent and not able to
speak until the day that these things will

60
00:04:31,277 --> 00:04:36,737
happen, because you didn’t believe my words,
which will be fulfilled in their proper

61
00:04:36,777 --> 00:04:37,677
time.”

62
00:04:37,937 --> 00:04:43,397
The people were waiting for Zacharias, and
they marvelled that he delayed in the temple.

63
00:04:44,457 --> 00:04:47,297
When he came out, he could not speak to
them.

64
00:04:47,563 --> 00:04:50,563
They perceived that he had seen a vision
in the temple.

65
00:04:51,843 --> 00:04:55,463
He continued making signs to them, and
remained mute.

66
00:04:56,583 --> 00:05:00,983
When the days of his service were
fulfilled, he departed to his house.

67
00:05:01,643 --> 00:05:08,183
After these days Elizabeth his wife conceived,
and she hid herself five months, saying,

68
00:05:09,083 --> 00:05:14,943
“Thus has the Lord done to me in the days
in which he looked at me, to take away my reproach

69
00:05:14,983 --> 00:05:15,883
amongst men.”

70
00:05:16,243 --> 00:05:22,823
Now in the sixth month, the angel Gabriel was
sent from God to a city of Galilee named

71
00:05:22,863 --> 00:05:29,503
Nazareth, to a virgin pledged to be married
to a man whose name was Joseph, of David’s

72
00:05:29,543 --> 00:05:30,443
house.

73
00:05:30,783 --> 00:05:32,183
The virgin’s name was Mary.

74
00:05:32,803 --> 00:05:38,003
Having come in, the angel said to her,
“Rejoice, you highly favoured one!

75
00:05:38,643 --> 00:05:39,763
The Lord is with you.

76
00:05:40,403 --> 00:05:42,083
Blessed are you amongst women!”

77
00:05:42,863 --> 00:05:48,803
But when she saw him, she was greatly
troubled at the saying, and considered what kind

78
00:05:48,843 --> 00:05:50,663
of salutation this might be.

79
00:05:51,923 --> 00:05:57,603
The angel said to her, “Don’t be afraid,
Mary, for you have found favour with God.

80
00:05:58,283 --> 00:06:04,663
Behold, you will conceive in your womb and give
birth to a son, and shall name him ‘Jesus.’

81
00:06:05,863 --> 00:06:09,583
He will be great and will be called the
Son of the Most High.

82
00:06:10,703 --> 00:06:16,243
The Lord God will give him the throne of
his father David, and he will reign over the

83
00:06:16,283 --> 00:06:17,543
house of Jacob forever.

84
00:06:18,363 --> 00:06:20,403
There will be no end to his Kingdom.”

85
00:06:21,303 --> 00:06:26,063
Mary said to the angel, “How can this be,
seeing I am a virgin?”

86
00:06:27,103 --> 00:06:33,423
The angel answered her, “The Holy Spirit will
come on you, and the power of the Most

87
00:06:33,463 --> 00:06:35,283
High will overshadow you.

88
00:06:35,883 --> 00:06:41,523
Therefore also the holy one who is born
from you will be called the Son of God.

89
00:06:42,663 --> 00:06:49,243
Behold, Elizabeth your relative also has
conceived a son in her old age; and

90
00:06:49,283 --> 00:06:53,563
this is the sixth month with her who was
called barren.

91
00:06:53,603 --> 00:06:56,163
For nothing spoken by God is impossible.”

92
00:06:57,123 --> 00:07:03,783
Mary said, “Behold, the servant of the
Lord; let it be done to me according to

93
00:07:03,823 --> 00:07:04,723
your word.”

94
00:07:05,603 --> 00:07:07,523
Then the angel departed from her.

95
00:07:07,842 --> 00:07:14,402
Mary arose in those days and went into the
hill country with haste, into a city of Judah,

96
00:07:15,262 --> 00:07:19,042
and entered into the house of Zacharias
and greeted Elizabeth.

97
00:07:20,082 --> 00:07:26,822
When Elizabeth heard Mary’s greeting, the baby
leapt in her womb; and Elizabeth was filled

98
00:07:26,862 --> 00:07:28,162
with the Holy Spirit.

99
00:07:28,822 --> 00:07:34,682
She called out with a loud voice and
said, “Blessed are you amongst women, and blessed

100
00:07:34,722 --> 00:07:36,162
is the fruit of your womb!

101
00:07:37,322 --> 00:07:41,582
Why am I so favoured, that the mother of
my Lord should come to me?

102
00:07:42,462 --> 00:07:48,502
For behold, when the voice of your greeting came
into my ears, the baby leapt in my womb

103
00:07:48,542 --> 00:07:49,442
for joy!

104
00:07:49,822 --> 00:07:54,562
Blessed is she who believed, for there will
be a fulfilment of the things which have

105
00:07:54,602 --> 00:07:56,362
been spoken to her from the Lord!”

106
00:07:57,302 --> 00:08:00,782
Mary said, “My soul magnifies the Lord.

107
00:08:01,442 --> 00:08:06,982
My spirit has rejoiced in God my Saviour, for
he has looked at the humble state of his

108
00:08:07,022 --> 00:08:07,922
servant.

109
00:08:08,022 --> 00:08:12,822
For behold, from now on, all generations
will call me blessed.

110
00:08:13,462 --> 00:08:17,162
For he who is mighty has done great things
for me.

111
00:08:18,282 --> 00:08:19,382
Holy is his name.

112
00:08:19,862 --> 00:08:24,742
His mercy is for generations and
generations on those who fear him.

113
00:08:25,062 --> 00:08:26,962
He has shown strength with his arm.

114
00:08:27,702 --> 00:08:30,982
He has scattered the proud in the
imagination of their hearts.

115
00:08:31,742 --> 00:08:36,082
He has put down princes from their
thrones, and has exalted the lowly.

116
00:08:37,062 --> 00:08:39,302
He has filled the hungry with good things.

117
00:08:40,022 --> 00:08:41,822
He has sent the rich away empty.

118
00:08:42,582 --> 00:08:48,702
He has given help to Israel, his servant,
that he might remember mercy, as he spoke to

119
00:08:48,742 --> 00:08:52,062
our fathers, to Abraham and his offspring
forever.”

120
00:08:52,902 --> 00:08:57,282
Mary stayed with her about three months,
and then returned to her house.

121
00:08:58,182 --> 00:09:03,982
Now the time that Elizabeth should give birth
was fulfilled, and she gave birth to a

122
00:09:04,022 --> 00:09:04,922
son.

123
00:09:05,322 --> 00:09:10,322
Her neighbours and her relatives heard that
the Lord had magnified his mercy towards

124
00:09:10,362 --> 00:09:12,522
her, and they rejoiced with her.

125
00:09:13,042 --> 00:09:18,182
On the eighth day, they came to circumcise
the child; and they would have called him

126
00:09:18,222 --> 00:09:20,942
Zacharias, after the name of his father.

127
00:09:21,922 --> 00:09:26,342
His mother answered, “Not so; but he will
be called John.”

128
00:09:26,891 --> 00:09:32,471
They said to her, “There is no one
amongst your relatives who is called by this name.”

129
00:09:33,311 --> 00:09:37,391
They made signs to his father, what he
would have him called.

130
00:09:38,391 --> 00:09:43,371
He asked for a writing tablet, and wrote,
“His name is John.”

131
00:09:44,571 --> 00:09:46,071
They all marvelled.

132
00:09:46,111 --> 00:09:52,791
His mouth was opened immediately and his
tongue freed, and he spoke, blessing God.

133
00:09:53,851 --> 00:09:59,811
Fear came on all who lived around them,
and all these sayings were talked about throughout

134
00:09:59,851 --> 00:10:01,991
all the hill country of Judea.

135
00:10:02,351 --> 00:10:08,531
All who heard them laid them up in
their heart, saying, “What then will this child be?”

136
00:10:09,311 --> 00:10:11,171
The hand of the Lord was with him.

137
00:10:11,891 --> 00:10:18,531
His father Zacharias was filled with
the Holy Spirit, and prophesied, saying, “Blessed

138
00:10:18,571 --> 00:10:25,211
be the Lord, the God of Israel, for he has
visited and redeemed his people; and

139
00:10:25,251 --> 00:10:31,551
has raised up a horn of salvation for us
in the house of his servant David (as he spoke

140
00:10:31,591 --> 00:10:38,031
by the mouth of his holy prophets who
have been from of old), salvation from our enemies

141
00:10:38,691 --> 00:10:44,451
and from the hand of all who hate
us; to show mercy towards our fathers, to remember

142
00:10:44,491 --> 00:10:50,951
his holy covenant, the oath which he swore
to Abraham our father, to grant to

143
00:10:50,991 --> 00:10:56,471
us that we, being delivered out of the
hand of our enemies, should serve him without

144
00:10:56,511 --> 00:11:01,991
fear, in holiness and righteousness before
him all the days of our life.

145
00:11:02,451 --> 00:11:08,391
And you, child, will be called a prophet of
the Most High; for you will go before the

146
00:11:08,431 --> 00:11:14,911
face of the Lord to prepare his ways,
to give knowledge of salvation to his people by

147
00:11:14,951 --> 00:11:21,191
the remission of their sins, because of the
tender mercy of our God, by which the dawn

148
00:11:21,231 --> 00:11:27,531
from on high will visit us, to shine on
those who sit in darkness and the shadow of death;

149
00:11:28,131 --> 00:11:30,431
to guide our feet into the way of peace.”

150
00:11:31,351 --> 00:11:37,811
The child was growing and becoming strong
in spirit, and was in the desert until the

151
00:11:37,851 --> 00:11:39,991
day of his public appearance to Israel.

152
00:11:41,491 --> 00:11:43,591
Luke, chapter two.

153
00:11:43,631 --> 00:11:49,811
Now in those days, a decree went out
from Caesar Augustus that all the world should be

154
00:11:49,851 --> 00:11:50,592
enrolled.

155
00:11:50,632 --> 00:11:54,972
This was the first enrolment made when
Quirinius was governor of Syria.

156
00:11:56,311 --> 00:12:00,452
All went to enrol themselves, everyone to
his own city.

157
00:12:01,092 --> 00:12:07,772
Joseph also went up from Galilee, out of
the city of Nazareth, into Judea, to

158
00:12:07,811 --> 00:12:13,691
David’s city, which is called Bethlehem, because he
was of the house and family of David,

159
00:12:14,372 --> 00:12:20,872
to enrol himself with Mary, who was pledged
to be married to him as wife, being pregnant.

160
00:12:21,691 --> 00:12:25,051
While they were there, the day had come
for her to give birth.

161
00:12:25,952 --> 00:12:28,272
She gave birth to her firstborn son.

162
00:12:29,152 --> 00:12:34,492
She wrapped him in bands of cloth and laid
him in a feeding trough, because there was

163
00:12:34,531 --> 00:12:36,132
no room for them in the inn.

164
00:12:36,732 --> 00:12:41,992
There were shepherds in the same country staying
in the field, and keeping watch by night

165
00:12:42,031 --> 00:12:42,931
over their flock.

166
00:12:44,232 --> 00:12:50,572
Behold, an angel of the Lord stood by them,
and the glory of the Lord shone around them,

167
00:12:50,992 --> 00:12:52,031
and they were terrified.

168
00:12:52,752 --> 00:12:59,292
The angel said to them, “Don’t be afraid,
for behold, I bring you good news of great

169
00:12:59,332 --> 00:13:01,872
joy which will be to all the people.

170
00:13:02,772 --> 00:13:09,012
For there is born to you today, in David’s
city, a Saviour, who is Christ the Lord.

171
00:13:09,612 --> 00:13:16,152
This is the sign to you: you will find a
baby wrapped in strips of cloth, lying in

172
00:13:16,191 --> 00:13:17,091
a feeding trough.”

173
00:13:17,332 --> 00:13:23,312
Suddenly, there was with the angel a
multitude of the heavenly army praising God and

174
00:13:23,352 --> 00:13:29,911
saying, “Glory to God in the highest, on
earth peace, good will towards men.”

175
00:13:30,691 --> 00:13:35,451
When the angels went away from them into
the sky, the shepherds said to one another,

176
00:13:36,291 --> 00:13:41,532
“Let’s go to Bethlehem, now, and see this
thing that has happened, which the Lord has

177
00:13:41,572 --> 00:13:42,632
made known to us.”

178
00:13:43,492 --> 00:13:49,492
They came with haste and found both Mary and
Joseph, and the baby was lying in the feeding

179
00:13:49,531 --> 00:13:50,431
trough.

180
00:13:50,572 --> 00:13:55,992
When they saw it, they publicised widely the
saying which was spoken to them about this

181
00:13:56,031 --> 00:13:56,931
child.

182
00:13:57,352 --> 00:14:01,852
All who heard it wondered at the things
which were spoken to them by the shepherds.

183
00:14:01,892 --> 00:14:06,772
But Mary kept all these sayings, pondering
them in her heart.

184
00:14:07,091 --> 00:14:12,671
The shepherds returned, glorifying and praising God
for all the things that they had

185
00:14:12,711 --> 00:14:15,891
heard and seen, just as it was told them.

186
00:14:16,571 --> 00:14:22,371
When eight days were fulfilled for the
circumcision of the child, his name was called

187
00:14:22,411 --> 00:14:27,551
Jesus, which was given by the angel before
he was conceived in the womb.

188
00:14:28,171 --> 00:14:33,651
When the days of their purification according
to the law of Moses were fulfilled, they

189
00:14:33,691 --> 00:14:39,451
brought him up to Jerusalem to present him to
the Lord (as it is written in the law of

190
00:14:39,491 --> 00:14:45,871
the Lord, “Every male who opens the womb shall
be called holy to the Lord”), and to offer

191
00:14:45,911 --> 00:14:51,651
a sacrifice according to that which is said in
the law of the Lord, “A pair of turtledoves,

192
00:14:51,691 --> 00:14:53,431
or two young pigeons.”

193
00:14:53,891 --> 00:14:58,271
Behold, there was a man in Jerusalem whose
name was Simeon.

194
00:14:58,731 --> 00:15:04,811
This man was righteous and devout, looking
for the consolation of Israel, and the Holy

195
00:15:04,851 --> 00:15:06,151
Spirit was on him.

196
00:15:06,971 --> 00:15:12,111
It had been revealed to him by the Holy
Spirit that he should not see death before he

197
00:15:12,151 --> 00:15:13,331
had seen the Lord’s Christ.

198
00:15:14,111 --> 00:15:16,211
He came in the Spirit into the temple.

199
00:15:17,111 --> 00:15:22,911
When the parents brought in the child,
Jesus, that they might do concerning him according

200
00:15:22,951 --> 00:15:29,571
to the custom of the law, then he received
him into his arms and blessed God, and

201
00:15:29,611 --> 00:15:35,591
said, “Now you are releasing your servant,
Master, according to your word, in peace;

202
00:15:36,111 --> 00:15:41,431
for my eyes have seen your salvation, which
you have prepared before the face of all

203
00:15:41,471 --> 00:15:47,491
peoples; a light for revelation to the
nations, and the glory of your people Israel.”

204
00:15:48,571 --> 00:15:53,591
Joseph and his mother were marvelling at
the things which were spoken concerning him.

205
00:15:54,211 --> 00:16:00,991
Simeon blessed them, and said to Mary,
his mother, “Behold, this child is appointed for

206
00:16:01,031 --> 00:16:06,451
the falling and the rising of many in
Israel, and for a sign which is spoken against.

207
00:16:07,071 --> 00:16:12,991
Yes, a sword will pierce through your own
soul, that the thoughts of many hearts may

208
00:16:13,031 --> 00:16:13,931
be revealed.”

209
00:16:14,064 --> 00:16:21,384
There was one Anna, a prophetess, the daughter
of Phanuel, of the tribe of Asher (she

210
00:16:21,424 --> 00:16:27,804
was of a great age, having lived with
a husband seven years from her virginity, and she

211
00:16:27,844 --> 00:16:34,324
had been a widow for about eighty-four
years), who didn’t depart from the temple, worshipping

212
00:16:34,364 --> 00:16:36,924
with fastings and petitions night and day.

213
00:16:37,404 --> 00:16:43,624
Coming up at that very hour, she gave thanks
to the Lord, and spoke of him to all those

214
00:16:43,664 --> 00:16:45,924
who were looking for redemption in
Jerusalem.

215
00:16:46,984 --> 00:16:52,384
When they had accomplished all things that were
according to the law of the Lord, they

216
00:16:52,424 --> 00:16:56,204
returned into Galilee, to their own city,
Nazareth.

217
00:16:56,924 --> 00:17:03,364
The child was growing, and was becoming
strong in spirit, being filled with wisdom, and

218
00:17:03,404 --> 00:17:05,304
the grace of God was upon him.

219
00:17:05,944 --> 00:17:10,584
His parents went every year to Jerusalem
at the feast of the Passover.

220
00:17:11,004 --> 00:17:15,944
When he was twelve years old, they went
up to Jerusalem according to the custom of the

221
00:17:15,984 --> 00:17:22,044
feast; and when they had fulfilled the days,
as they were returning, the boy Jesus stayed

222
00:17:22,084 --> 00:17:23,124
behind in Jerusalem.

223
00:17:24,324 --> 00:17:30,364
Joseph and his mother didn’t know it, but
supposing him to be in the company, they went

224
00:17:30,404 --> 00:17:34,744
a day’s journey; and they looked for him
amongst their relatives and acquaintances.

225
00:17:35,884 --> 00:17:39,984
When they didn’t find him, they returned
to Jerusalem, looking for him.

226
00:17:41,044 --> 00:17:46,084
After three days they found him in the
temple, sitting in the middle of the teachers,

227
00:17:46,884 --> 00:17:49,364
both listening to them and asking them
questions.

228
00:17:50,064 --> 00:17:53,624
All who heard him were amazed at his
understanding and his answers.

229
00:17:54,384 --> 00:18:00,984
When they saw him, they were astonished;
and his mother said to him, “Son, why have

230
00:18:01,024 --> 00:18:02,264
you treated us this way?

231
00:18:03,084 --> 00:18:07,004
Behold, your father and I were anxiously
looking for you.”

232
00:18:07,804 --> 00:18:10,904
He said to them, “Why were you looking for
me?

233
00:18:11,584 --> 00:18:14,504
Didn’t you know that I must be in my
Father’s house?”

234
00:18:15,064 --> 00:18:17,984
They didn’t understand the saying which he
spoke to them.

235
00:18:18,684 --> 00:18:21,344
And he went down with them and came to
Nazareth.

236
00:18:21,984 --> 00:18:26,384
He was subject to them, and his mother
kept all these sayings in her heart.

237
00:18:26,676 --> 00:18:32,176
And Jesus increased in wisdom and stature,
and in favour with God and men.

238
00:18:33,216 --> 00:18:36,136
Luke, chapter three.

239
00:18:36,176 --> 00:18:42,556
Now in the fifteenth year of the
reign of Tiberius Caesar, Pontius Pilate being governor

240
00:18:42,596 --> 00:18:48,896
of Judea, and Herod being tetrarch of
Galilee, and his brother Philip tetrarch of the

241
00:18:48,936 --> 00:18:55,576
region of Ituraea and Trachonitis, and
Lysanias tetrarch of Abilene, during the high

242
00:18:55,616 --> 00:19:02,316
priesthood of Annas and Caiaphas, the word
of God came to John, the son of Zacharias,

243
00:19:02,636 --> 00:19:03,536
in the wilderness.

244
00:19:04,056 --> 00:19:09,796
He came into all the region around
the Jordan, preaching the baptism of repentance for

245
00:19:09,836 --> 00:19:10,816
remission of sins.

246
00:19:11,896 --> 00:19:17,516
As it is written in the book of the
words of Isaiah the prophet, “The voice of one crying

247
00:19:17,556 --> 00:19:20,756
in the wilderness, ‘Make ready the way of
the Lord.

248
00:19:21,216 --> 00:19:22,756
Make his paths straight.

249
00:19:23,376 --> 00:19:25,016
Every valley will be filled.

250
00:19:25,856 --> 00:19:28,356
Every mountain and hill will be brought
low.

251
00:19:29,316 --> 00:19:32,976
The crooked will become straight, and the
rough ways smooth.

252
00:19:34,056 --> 00:19:39,896
All flesh will see God’s salvation.’” He
said therefore to the multitudes who went out

253
00:19:39,936 --> 00:19:46,556
to be baptised by him, “You offspring of
vipers, who warned you to flee from the wrath

254
00:19:46,596 --> 00:19:47,496
to come?

255
00:19:48,216 --> 00:19:53,996
Therefore produce fruits worthy of repentance,
and don’t begin to say amongst yourselves,

256
00:19:54,716 --> 00:19:59,956
‘We have Abraham for our father;’ for I tell
you that God is able to raise up children

257
00:19:59,996 --> 00:20:02,056
to Abraham from these stones!

258
00:20:03,196 --> 00:20:07,016
Even now the axe also lies at the root of
the trees.

259
00:20:07,916 --> 00:20:13,356
Every tree therefore that doesn’t produce
good fruit is cut down and thrown into the

260
00:20:13,396 --> 00:20:14,296
fire.”

261
00:20:14,616 --> 00:20:18,076
The multitudes asked him, “What then must
we do?”

262
00:20:18,716 --> 00:20:24,196
He answered them, “He who has two coats,
let him give to him who has none.

263
00:20:24,996 --> 00:20:27,616
He who has food, let him do likewise.”

264
00:20:28,976 --> 00:20:35,636
Tax collectors also came to be baptised, and
they said to him, “Teacher, what must we

265
00:20:35,676 --> 00:20:36,576
do?”

266
00:20:36,876 --> 00:20:41,316
He said to them, “Collect no more than
that which is appointed to you.”

267
00:20:41,896 --> 00:20:45,416
Soldiers also asked him, saying, “What
about us?

268
00:20:45,956 --> 00:20:46,956
What must we do?”

269
00:20:47,936 --> 00:20:54,376
He said to them, “Extort from no
one by violence, neither accuse anyone wrongfully.

270
00:20:54,727 --> 00:20:56,387
Be content with your wages.”

271
00:20:57,027 --> 00:21:03,207
As the people were in expectation, and
all men reasoned in their hearts concerning John,

272
00:21:03,947 --> 00:21:10,907
whether perhaps he was the Christ, John
answered them all, “I indeed baptise

273
00:21:10,947 --> 00:21:17,367
you with water, but he comes who is mightier
than I, the strap of whose sandals I am

274
00:21:17,407 --> 00:21:18,587
not worthy to loosen.

275
00:21:18,627 --> 00:21:22,367
He will baptise you in the Holy Spirit and
fire.

276
00:21:23,407 --> 00:21:28,867
His winnowing fan is in his hand,
and he will thoroughly cleanse his threshing floor,

277
00:21:29,827 --> 00:21:35,427
and will gather the wheat into his barn;
but he will burn up the chaff with unquenchable

278
00:21:35,467 --> 00:21:36,367
fire.”

279
00:21:36,527 --> 00:21:42,687
Then with many other exhortations he preached
good news to the people, but Herod the

280
00:21:42,727 --> 00:21:49,367
tetrarch, being reproved by him for Herodias,
his brother’s wife, and for all the evil

281
00:21:49,407 --> 00:21:55,867
things which Herod had done, added this
also to them all, that he shut up John in

282
00:21:55,907 --> 00:21:56,807
prison.

283
00:21:56,947 --> 00:22:02,487
Now when all the people were baptised,
Jesus also had been baptised and was praying.

284
00:22:03,427 --> 00:22:09,347
The sky was opened, and the Holy Spirit descended
in a bodily form like a dove on him;

285
00:22:09,387 --> 00:22:14,687
and a voice came out of the sky, saying
“You are my beloved Son.

286
00:22:15,407 --> 00:22:16,947
In you I am well pleased.”

287
00:22:17,441 --> 00:22:24,061
Jesus himself, when he began to teach, was
about thirty years old, being

288
00:22:24,101 --> 00:22:31,121
the son (as was supposed) of Joseph, the
son of Heli, the son of Matthat,

289
00:22:31,161 --> 00:22:37,681
the son of Levi, the son of Melchi, the
son of Jannai, the son of Joseph, the son

290
00:22:37,721 --> 00:22:44,121
of Mattathias, the son of Amos, the son of
Nahum, the son of Esli, the son of Naggai,

291
00:22:44,161 --> 00:22:49,861
the son of Maath, the son of Mattathias, the
son of Semein, the son of Joseph, the son

292
00:22:49,901 --> 00:22:56,221
of Judah, the son of Joanan, the son of
Rhesa, the son of Zerubbabel, the son of Shealtiel,

293
00:22:56,261 --> 00:23:02,161
the son of Neri, the son of Melchi, the son
of Addi, the son of Cosam, the son of Elmodam,

294
00:23:02,201 --> 00:23:08,641
the son of Er, the son of Jose, the son
of Eliezer, the son of Jorim, the son of Matthat,

295
00:23:08,681 --> 00:23:14,541
the son of Levi, the son of Simeon, the son
of Judah, the son of Joseph, the son of Jonan,

296
00:23:14,861 --> 00:23:20,221
the son of Eliakim, the son of Melea, the
son of Menan, the son of Mattatha, the son

297
00:23:20,261 --> 00:23:26,401
of Nathan, the son of David, the son of
Jesse, the son of Obed, the son of Boaz, the

298
00:23:26,441 --> 00:23:32,101
son of Salmon, the son of Nahshon, the son
of Amminadab, the son of Aram, the son of

299
00:23:32,141 --> 00:23:38,041
Hezron, the son of Perez, the son of Judah,
the son of Jacob, the son of Isaac, the son

300
00:23:38,081 --> 00:23:44,201
of Abraham, the son of Terah, the son of
Nahor, the son of Serug, the son of Reu, the

301
00:23:44,241 --> 00:23:50,261
son of Peleg, the son of Eber, the son
of Shelah, the son of Cainan, the son of Arphaxad,

302
00:23:50,301 --> 00:23:55,561
the son of Shem, the son of Noah, the
son of Lamech, the son of Methuselah, the son of

303
00:23:55,601 --> 00:24:01,321
Enoch, the son of Jared, the son of Mahalaleel,
the son of Cainan, the son of Enos, the

304
00:24:01,361 --> 00:24:04,361
son of Seth, the son of Adam, the son of
God.

305
00:24:05,321 --> 00:24:07,921
Luke, chapter four.

306
00:24:07,961 --> 00:24:14,441
Jesus, full of the Holy Spirit, returned from
the Jordan and was led by the Spirit into

307
00:24:14,481 --> 00:24:18,421
the wilderness for forty days, being
tempted by the devil.

308
00:24:19,341 --> 00:24:20,761
He ate nothing in those days.

309
00:24:21,821 --> 00:24:24,921
Afterward, when they were completed, he
was hungry.

310
00:24:25,621 --> 00:24:31,541
The devil said to him, “If you are the
Son of God, command this stone to become bread.”

311
00:24:31,967 --> 00:24:38,345
Jesus answered him, saying, “It is written, ‘Man
shall not live by bread alone, but by

312
00:24:38,385 --> 00:24:45,170
every word of God.’” The devil, leading him
up on a high mountain, showed him all the

313
00:24:45,210 --> 00:24:48,784
kingdoms of the world in a moment of time.

314
00:24:48,824 --> 00:24:55,609
The devil said to him, “I will give you
all this authority and their glory, for it

315
00:24:55,649 --> 00:25:00,829
has been delivered to me, and I give it to
whomever I want.

316
00:25:00,869 --> 00:25:05,647
If you therefore will worship before me,
it will all be yours.”

317
00:25:05,687 --> 00:25:08,667
Jesus answered him, “Get behind me, Satan!

318
00:25:09,387 --> 00:25:14,607
For it is written, ‘You shall worship the
Lord your God, and you shall serve him only.’”

319
00:25:15,347 --> 00:25:21,667
He led him to Jerusalem and set him on
the pinnacle of the temple, and said to him, “If

320
00:25:21,707 --> 00:25:28,007
you are the Son of God, cast yourself down
from here, for it is written, ‘He will put

321
00:25:28,047 --> 00:25:34,387
his angels in charge of you, to guard you;’
and, ‘On their hands they will bear you up,

322
00:25:34,767 --> 00:25:41,727
lest perhaps you dash your foot against a
stone.’” Jesus answering, said to him, “It

323
00:25:41,767 --> 00:25:47,847
has been said, ‘You shall not tempt the
Lord your God.’” When the devil had completed

324
00:25:47,887 --> 00:25:51,887
every temptation, he departed from him
until another time.

325
00:25:52,647 --> 00:25:58,587
Jesus returned in the power of the Spirit
into Galilee, and news about him spread through

326
00:25:58,627 --> 00:26:00,027
all the surrounding area.

327
00:26:01,347 --> 00:26:04,947
He taught in their synagogues, being
glorified by all.

328
00:26:05,967 --> 00:26:08,907
He came to Nazareth, where he had been
brought up.

329
00:26:09,547 --> 00:26:15,187
He entered, as was his custom, into the
synagogue on the Sabbath day, and stood up to

330
00:26:15,227 --> 00:26:16,127
read.

331
00:26:16,487 --> 00:26:19,347
The book of the prophet Isaiah was handed
to him.

332
00:26:20,187 --> 00:26:25,547
He opened the book, and found the place
where it was written, “The Spirit of the Lord

333
00:26:25,587 --> 00:26:30,147
is on me, because he has anointed me to
preach good news to the poor.

334
00:26:30,827 --> 00:26:37,207
He has sent me to heal the broken
hearted, to proclaim release to the captives, recovering

335
00:26:37,247 --> 00:26:43,647
of sight to the blind, to deliver those
who are crushed, and to proclaim the acceptable

336
00:26:43,687 --> 00:26:44,927
year of the Lord.”

337
00:26:45,467 --> 00:26:49,707
He closed the book, gave it back to the
attendant, and sat down.

338
00:26:49,747 --> 00:26:53,507
The eyes of all in the synagogue were
fastened on him.

339
00:26:53,868 --> 00:27:00,088
He began to tell them, “Today, this
Scripture has been fulfilled in your hearing.”

340
00:27:01,008 --> 00:27:06,588
All testified about him and wondered at
the gracious words which proceeded out of his

341
00:27:06,628 --> 00:27:10,808
mouth; and they said, “Isn’t this Joseph’s
son?”

342
00:27:11,508 --> 00:27:17,368
He said to them, “Doubtless you will
tell me this proverb, ‘Physician, heal yourself!

343
00:27:18,048 --> 00:27:24,808
Whatever we have heard done at Capernaum,
do also here in your hometown.’” He said,

344
00:27:25,568 --> 00:27:30,408
“Most certainly I tell you, no prophet is
acceptable in his hometown.

345
00:27:31,168 --> 00:27:37,268
But truly I tell you, there were many widows
in Israel in the days of Elijah, when the

346
00:27:37,308 --> 00:27:43,408
sky was shut up three years and six months,
when a great famine came over all the land.

347
00:27:43,448 --> 00:27:50,188
Elijah was sent to none of them, except to
Zarephath, in the land of Sidon, to a woman

348
00:27:50,228 --> 00:27:51,128
who was a widow.

349
00:27:51,688 --> 00:27:57,568
There were many lepers in Israel in the time
of Elisha the prophet, yet not one of them

350
00:27:57,608 --> 00:28:00,748
was cleansed, except Naaman, the Syrian.”

351
00:28:01,888 --> 00:28:06,668
They were all filled with wrath in the
synagogue as they heard these things.

352
00:28:07,348 --> 00:28:12,928
They rose up, threw him out of the city, and
led him to the brow of the hill that their

353
00:28:12,968 --> 00:28:16,768
city was built on, that they might throw
him off the cliff.

354
00:28:17,828 --> 00:28:21,728
But he, passing through the middle of
them, went his way.

355
00:28:22,168 --> 00:28:25,708
He came down to Capernaum, a city of
Galilee.

356
00:28:26,168 --> 00:28:31,988
He was teaching them on the Sabbath day,
and they were astonished at his teaching, for

357
00:28:32,028 --> 00:28:33,528
his word was with authority.

358
00:28:34,668 --> 00:28:40,828
In the synagogue there was a man who had
a spirit of an unclean demon; and he cried out

359
00:28:40,868 --> 00:28:43,808
with a loud voice, saying, “Ah!

360
00:28:44,428 --> 00:28:47,228
what have we to do with you, Jesus of
Nazareth?

361
00:28:47,828 --> 00:28:49,428
Have you come to destroy us?

362
00:28:50,268 --> 00:28:53,488
I know who you are: the Holy One of God!”

363
00:28:54,488 --> 00:28:58,908
Jesus rebuked him, saying, “Be silent and
come out of him!”

364
00:28:59,908 --> 00:29:05,128
When the demon had thrown him down in the
middle of them, he came out of him, having

365
00:29:05,168 --> 00:29:06,268
done him no harm.

366
00:29:06,908 --> 00:29:13,488
Amazement came on all and they spoke
together, one with another, saying, “What is

367
00:29:13,528 --> 00:29:14,428
this word?

368
00:29:15,008 --> 00:29:20,328
For with authority and power he commands
the unclean spirits, and they come out!”

369
00:29:20,635 --> 00:29:24,755
News about him went out into every place
of the surrounding region.

370
00:29:26,095 --> 00:29:29,815
He rose up from the synagogue and entered
into Simon’s house.

371
00:29:31,175 --> 00:29:36,495
Simon’s mother-in-law was afflicted with a great
fever, and they begged him to help her.

372
00:29:36,915 --> 00:29:40,775
He stood over her and rebuked the fever,
and it left her.

373
00:29:41,695 --> 00:29:43,835
Immediately she rose up and served them.

374
00:29:44,515 --> 00:29:50,815
When the sun was setting, all those who
had any sick with various diseases brought them

375
00:29:50,855 --> 00:29:55,875
to him; and he laid his hands on every one
of them, and healed them.

376
00:29:56,835 --> 00:30:03,435
Demons also came out of many, crying out
and saying, “You are the Christ, the Son

377
00:30:03,475 --> 00:30:04,375
of God!”

378
00:30:04,655 --> 00:30:09,995
Rebuking them, he didn’t allow them to speak,
because they knew that he was the Christ.

379
00:30:11,075 --> 00:30:17,815
When it was day, he departed and went
into an uninhabited place and the multitudes looked

380
00:30:17,855 --> 00:30:23,575
for him, and came to him, and held on
to him, so that he wouldn’t go away from them.

381
00:30:24,095 --> 00:30:29,615
But he said to them, “I must preach the
good news of God’s Kingdom to the other cities

382
00:30:29,655 --> 00:30:30,555
also.

383
00:30:30,935 --> 00:30:32,975
For this reason I have been sent.”

384
00:30:34,055 --> 00:30:36,935
He was preaching in the synagogues of
Galilee.

385
00:30:37,535 --> 00:30:39,675
Luke, chapter five.

386
00:30:39,715 --> 00:30:45,495
Now while the multitude pressed on him and
heard the word of God, he was standing by

387
00:30:45,535 --> 00:30:47,695
the lake of Gennesaret.

388
00:30:47,735 --> 00:30:53,775
He saw two boats standing by the lake, but
the fishermen had gone out of them and were

389
00:30:53,815 --> 00:30:54,715
washing their nets.

390
00:30:55,535 --> 00:31:00,775
He entered into one of the boats, which was
Simon’s, and asked him to put out a little

391
00:31:00,815 --> 00:31:01,715
from the land.

392
00:31:02,475 --> 00:31:05,855
He sat down and taught the multitudes from
the boat.

393
00:31:06,735 --> 00:31:13,015
When he had finished speaking, he said to
Simon, “Put out into the deep and let down

394
00:31:13,055 --> 00:31:14,295
your nets for a catch.”

395
00:31:15,015 --> 00:31:21,595
Simon answered him, “Master, we worked all
night and caught nothing; but

396
00:31:21,635 --> 00:31:23,935
at your word I will let down the net.”

397
00:31:24,955 --> 00:31:30,575
When they had done this, they caught a
great multitude of fish, and their net was breaking.

398
00:31:31,635 --> 00:31:36,155
They beckoned to their partners in the other
boat, that they should come and help them.

399
00:31:36,675 --> 00:31:40,535
They came and filled both boats, so that
they began to sink.

400
00:31:40,940 --> 00:31:47,500
But Simon Peter, when he saw it, fell down
at Jesus’ knees, saying, “Depart

401
00:31:47,540 --> 00:31:51,040
from me, for I am a sinful man, Lord.”

402
00:31:51,080 --> 00:31:56,640
For he was amazed, and all who were with
him, at the catch of fish which they had caught;

403
00:31:57,500 --> 00:32:03,260
and so also were James and John, sons of
Zebedee, who were partners with Simon.

404
00:32:04,000 --> 00:32:06,720
Jesus said to Simon, “Don’t be afraid.

405
00:32:06,880 --> 00:32:10,080
From now on you will be catching people
alive.”

406
00:32:10,940 --> 00:32:16,120
When they had brought their boats to land,
they left everything, and followed him.

407
00:32:16,540 --> 00:32:21,460
While he was in one of the cities, behold,
there was a man full of leprosy.

408
00:32:22,100 --> 00:32:28,800
When he saw Jesus, he fell on his face and
begged him, saying, “Lord, if you want to,

409
00:32:29,200 --> 00:32:30,300
you can make me clean.”

410
00:32:31,020 --> 00:32:35,600
He stretched out his hand and touched him,
saying, “I want to.

411
00:32:35,980 --> 00:32:36,940
Be made clean.”

412
00:32:37,860 --> 00:32:40,060
Immediately the leprosy left him.

413
00:32:40,100 --> 00:32:47,020
He commanded him to tell no one, “But go
your way and show yourself to the priest, and

414
00:32:47,060 --> 00:32:52,340
offer for your cleansing according to what
Moses commanded, for a testimony to them.”

415
00:32:52,920 --> 00:32:58,580
But the report concerning him spread much
more, and great multitudes came together to

416
00:32:58,620 --> 00:33:01,720
hear and to be healed by him of their
infirmities.

417
00:33:02,460 --> 00:33:05,480
But he withdrew himself into the desert
and prayed.

418
00:33:06,180 --> 00:33:11,600
On one of those days, he was teaching;
and there were Pharisees and teachers of the law

419
00:33:11,640 --> 00:33:17,020
sitting by who had come out of every
village of Galilee, Judea, and Jerusalem.

420
00:33:18,360 --> 00:33:21,220
The power of the Lord was with him to heal
them.

421
00:33:22,060 --> 00:33:28,080
Behold, men brought a paralysed man on a cot,
and they sought to bring him in to lay

422
00:33:28,120 --> 00:33:29,020
before Jesus.

423
00:33:29,560 --> 00:33:34,880
Not finding a way to bring him in because
of the multitude, they went up to the housetop

424
00:33:34,920 --> 00:33:39,860
and let him down through the tiles with
his cot into the middle before Jesus.

425
00:33:40,960 --> 00:33:46,360
Seeing their faith, he said to him, “Man,
your sins are forgiven you.”

426
00:33:46,860 --> 00:33:53,520
The scribes and the Pharisees began to
reason, saying, “Who is this who speaks blasphemies?

427
00:33:54,160 --> 00:33:56,520
Who can forgive sins, but God alone?”

428
00:33:57,160 --> 00:34:03,640
But Jesus, perceiving their thoughts, answered them,
“Why are you reasoning so in your

429
00:34:03,680 --> 00:34:04,352
hearts?

430
00:34:04,392 --> 00:34:11,092
Which is easier to say, ‘Your sins are
forgiven you,’ or to say, ‘Arise and walk?’

431
00:34:12,212 --> 00:34:17,932
But that you may know that the Son of
Man has authority on earth to forgive sins,” he

432
00:34:17,972 --> 00:34:24,452
said to the paralysed man, “I tell you,
arise, take up your cot, and go to

433
00:34:24,492 --> 00:34:25,392
your house.”

434
00:34:25,712 --> 00:34:31,492
Immediately he rose up before them, and took
up that which he was laying on, and departed

435
00:34:31,532 --> 00:34:34,272
to his house, glorifying God.

436
00:34:35,252 --> 00:34:38,972
Amazement took hold on all, and they
glorified God.

437
00:34:39,712 --> 00:34:44,672
They were filled with fear, saying, “We
have seen strange things today.”

438
00:34:45,252 --> 00:34:50,932
After these things he went out and saw
a tax collector named Levi sitting at the tax

439
00:34:50,972 --> 00:34:54,072
office, and said to him, “Follow me!”

440
00:34:54,812 --> 00:34:58,072
He left everything, and rose up and
followed him.

441
00:34:59,092 --> 00:35:01,552
Levi made a great feast for him in his
house.

442
00:35:02,172 --> 00:35:06,692
There was a great crowd of tax collectors
and others who were reclining with them.

443
00:35:07,512 --> 00:35:13,392
Their scribes and the Pharisees murmured against
his disciples, saying, “Why do you eat

444
00:35:13,432 --> 00:35:15,752
and drink with the tax collectors and
sinners?”

445
00:35:16,472 --> 00:35:22,312
Jesus answered them, “Those who are healthy have
no need for a physician, but those who

446
00:35:22,352 --> 00:35:23,252
are sick do.

447
00:35:23,752 --> 00:35:27,532
I have not come to call the righteous, but
sinners, to repentance.”

448
00:35:28,332 --> 00:35:34,832
They said to him, “Why do John’s disciples
often fast and pray, likewise also

449
00:35:34,872 --> 00:35:39,072
the disciples of the Pharisees, but yours
eat and drink?”

450
00:35:40,172 --> 00:35:45,372
He said to them, “Can you make the
friends of the bridegroom fast while the bridegroom

451
00:35:45,412 --> 00:35:46,312
is with them?

452
00:35:46,672 --> 00:35:50,292
But the days will come when the bridegroom
will be taken away from them.

453
00:35:51,072 --> 00:35:53,032
Then they will fast in those days.”

454
00:35:54,192 --> 00:35:56,012
He also told a parable to them.

455
00:35:56,792 --> 00:36:02,472
“No one puts a piece from a new garment on
an old garment, or else he will tear the new,

456
00:36:02,952 --> 00:36:06,372
and also the piece from the new will not
match the old.

457
00:36:07,112 --> 00:36:13,212
No one puts new wine into old wine skins,
or else the new wine will burst the skins,

458
00:36:13,252 --> 00:36:16,652
and it will be spilled and the skins will
be destroyed.

459
00:36:16,692 --> 00:36:22,352
But new wine must be put into fresh wine
skins, and both are preserved.

460
00:36:22,833 --> 00:36:29,493
No man having drunk old wine immediately
desires new, for he says, ‘The

461
00:36:29,533 --> 00:36:33,913
old is better.’” Luke, chapter six.

462
00:36:33,953 --> 00:36:39,113
Now on the second Sabbath after the first,
he was going through the grain fields.

463
00:36:39,733 --> 00:36:44,693
His disciples plucked the heads of grain
and ate, rubbing them in their hands.

464
00:36:45,573 --> 00:36:51,193
But some of the Pharisees said to them, “Why
do you do that which is not lawful to do

465
00:36:51,233 --> 00:36:52,393
on the Sabbath day?”

466
00:36:52,833 --> 00:36:59,153
Jesus, answering them, said, “Haven’t you
read what David did when he was hungry, he

467
00:36:59,193 --> 00:37:05,283
and those who were with him, how he entered
into God’s house, and took and ate the show

468
00:37:05,323 --> 00:37:11,113
bread, and gave also to those who were with
him, which is not lawful to eat except for

469
00:37:11,153 --> 00:37:12,053
the priests alone?”

470
00:37:12,773 --> 00:37:16,633
He said to them, “The Son of Man is lord
of the Sabbath.”

471
00:37:17,573 --> 00:37:22,873
It also happened on another Sabbath that
he entered into the synagogue and taught.

472
00:37:23,873 --> 00:37:27,513
There was a man there, and his right hand
was withered.

473
00:37:28,093 --> 00:37:33,173
The scribes and the Pharisees watched him, to
see whether he would heal on the Sabbath,

474
00:37:33,213 --> 00:37:36,713
that they might find an accusation against
him.

475
00:37:37,553 --> 00:37:43,533
But he knew their thoughts; and he said to
the man who had the withered hand, “Rise up

476
00:37:43,573 --> 00:37:44,793
and stand in the middle.”

477
00:37:45,173 --> 00:37:46,253
He arose and stood.

478
00:37:46,973 --> 00:37:53,233
Then Jesus said to them, “I will ask you
something: Is it lawful on the Sabbath to do

479
00:37:53,273 --> 00:37:54,773
good, or to do harm?

480
00:37:55,493 --> 00:37:57,333
To save a life, or to kill?”

481
00:37:58,193 --> 00:38:03,073
He looked around at them all, and said to
the man, “Stretch out your hand.”

482
00:38:03,533 --> 00:38:07,513
He did, and his hand was restored as sound
as the other.

483
00:38:08,133 --> 00:38:13,073
But they were filled with rage, and talked
with one another about what they might do

484
00:38:13,113 --> 00:38:13,613
to Jesus.

485
00:38:13,653 --> 00:38:20,373
In these days, he went out to the mountain
to pray, and he continued all night

486
00:38:20,413 --> 00:38:21,493
in prayer to God.

487
00:38:21,894 --> 00:38:28,494
When it was day, he called his disciples,
and from them he chose twelve, whom he also

488
00:38:28,534 --> 00:38:35,434
named apostles: Simon, whom he also named
Peter; Andrew, his

489
00:38:35,474 --> 00:38:42,514
brother; James; John; Philip; Bartholomew;
Matthew; Thomas;

490
00:38:44,094 --> 00:38:50,674
James the son of Alphaeus; Simon who was
called the Zealot; Judas the son of James;

491
00:38:51,374 --> 00:38:54,634
and Judas Iscariot, who also became a
traitor.

492
00:38:55,434 --> 00:39:01,614
He came down with them and stood on a
level place, with a crowd of his disciples and

493
00:39:01,654 --> 00:39:07,794
a great number of the people from all Judea
and Jerusalem and the sea coast of Tyre and

494
00:39:07,834 --> 00:39:13,954
Sidon, who came to hear him and to be
healed of their diseases, as well as those who

495
00:39:13,994 --> 00:39:17,794
were troubled by unclean spirits; and they
were being healed.

496
00:39:18,574 --> 00:39:24,634
All the multitude sought to touch him, for
power came out of him and healed them all.

497
00:39:25,934 --> 00:39:32,814
He lifted up his eyes to his disciples,
and said: “Blessed are you who are poor, for

498
00:39:32,854 --> 00:39:34,194
God’s Kingdom is yours.

499
00:39:35,274 --> 00:39:38,494
Blessed are you who hunger now, for you
will be filled.

500
00:39:39,214 --> 00:39:42,294
Blessed are you who weep now, for you will
laugh.

501
00:39:43,234 --> 00:39:48,694
Blessed are you when men hate you, and
when they exclude and mock you, and throw out

502
00:39:48,734 --> 00:39:51,754
your name as evil, for the Son of Man’s
sake.

503
00:39:52,354 --> 00:39:58,934
Rejoice in that day and leap for joy, for
behold, your reward is great in heaven,

504
00:39:59,894 --> 00:40:02,594
for their fathers did the same thing to
the prophets.

505
00:40:03,834 --> 00:40:05,714
“But woe to you who are rich!

506
00:40:06,434 --> 00:40:08,154
For you have received your consolation.

507
00:40:09,114 --> 00:40:13,254
Woe to you, you who are full now, for you
will be hungry.

508
00:40:13,894 --> 00:40:17,594
Woe to you who laugh now, for you will
mourn and weep.

509
00:40:18,514 --> 00:40:24,354
Woe, when men speak well of you, for their
fathers did the same thing to the false prophets.

510
00:40:25,534 --> 00:40:32,334
“But I tell you who hear: love your enemies,
do good to those who hate you, bless those

511
00:40:32,374 --> 00:40:35,794
who curse you, and pray for those who
mistreat you.

512
00:40:36,334 --> 00:40:42,674
To him who strikes you on the cheek, offer
also the other; and from him who takes away

513
00:40:42,714 --> 00:40:45,814
your cloak, don’t withhold your coat also.

514
00:40:46,674 --> 00:40:52,754
Give to everyone who asks you, and don’t ask
him who takes away your goods to give them

515
00:40:52,794 --> 00:40:53,694
back again.

516
00:40:53,814 --> 00:40:58,094
“As you would like people to do to you, do
exactly so to them.

517
00:40:59,234 --> 00:41:03,494
“If you love those who love you, what
credit is that to you?

518
00:41:04,254 --> 00:41:07,114
For even sinners love those who love them.

519
00:41:07,554 --> 00:41:12,674
If you do good to those who do good to
you, what credit is that to you?

520
00:41:13,434 --> 00:41:15,314
For even sinners do the same.

521
00:41:16,034 --> 00:41:21,354
If you lend to those from whom you hope to
receive, what credit is that to you?

522
00:41:22,314 --> 00:41:26,394
Even sinners lend to sinners, to receive
back as much.

523
00:41:27,334 --> 00:41:34,034
But love your enemies, and do good, and
lend, expecting nothing back; and

524
00:41:34,074 --> 00:41:39,674
your reward will be great, and you will be
children of the Most High; for he is kind

525
00:41:39,714 --> 00:41:41,754
towards the unthankful and evil.

526
00:41:42,854 --> 00:41:47,414
“Therefore be merciful, even as your
Father is also merciful.

527
00:41:47,994 --> 00:41:50,414
Don’t judge, and you won’t be judged.

528
00:41:51,314 --> 00:41:53,634
Don’t condemn, and you won’t be condemned.

529
00:41:54,714 --> 00:41:57,134
Set free, and you will be set free.

530
00:41:57,714 --> 00:42:04,814
“Give, and it will be given to
you: good measure, pressed down, shaken together, and

531
00:42:04,854 --> 00:42:07,194
running over, will be given to you.

532
00:42:07,954 --> 00:42:12,374
For with the same measure you measure it
will be measured back to you.”

533
00:42:14,734 --> 00:42:15,554
He spoke a parable to them.

534
00:42:15,594 --> 00:42:16,674
“Can the blind guide the blind?

535
00:42:17,514 --> 00:42:19,454
Won’t they both fall into a pit?

536
00:42:20,114 --> 00:42:26,454
A disciple is not above his teacher, but
everyone when he is fully trained will be like

537
00:42:26,494 --> 00:42:27,394
his teacher.

538
00:42:28,094 --> 00:42:33,654
Why do you see the speck of chaff that
is in your brother’s eye, but don’t consider the

539
00:42:33,694 --> 00:42:35,254
beam that is in your own eye?

540
00:42:35,814 --> 00:42:41,874
Or how can you tell your brother, ‘Brother,
let me remove the speck of chaff that is

541
00:42:41,914 --> 00:42:46,834
in your eye,’ when you yourself don’t see
the beam that is in your own eye?

542
00:42:47,714 --> 00:42:48,714
You hypocrite!

543
00:42:49,094 --> 00:42:55,154
First remove the beam from your own eye, and
then you can see clearly to remove the speck

544
00:42:55,194 --> 00:42:57,194
of chaff that is in your brother’s eye.

545
00:42:57,534 --> 00:43:03,674
“For there is no good tree that produces
rotten fruit, nor again a rotten tree that produces

546
00:43:03,714 --> 00:43:04,614
good fruit.

547
00:43:05,374 --> 00:43:07,974
For each tree is known by its own fruit.

548
00:43:08,574 --> 00:43:14,574
For people don’t gather figs from thorns, nor
do they gather grapes from a bramble bush.

549
00:43:14,904 --> 00:43:21,103
The good man out of the good treasure of
his heart brings out that which is good, and

550
00:43:21,143 --> 00:43:27,524
the evil man out of the evil treasure of
his heart brings out that which is evil, for

551
00:43:27,563 --> 00:43:31,004
out of the abundance of the heart, his
mouth speaks.

552
00:43:31,944 --> 00:43:36,784
“Why do you call me, ‘Lord, Lord,’ and
don’t do the things which I say?

553
00:43:37,844 --> 00:43:44,284
Everyone who comes to me, and hears my words
and does them, I will show you who he is

554
00:43:44,324 --> 00:43:45,224
like.

555
00:43:45,444 --> 00:43:51,904
He is like a man building a house, who dug
and went deep and laid a foundation on

556
00:43:51,944 --> 00:43:52,284
the rock.

557
00:43:52,324 --> 00:43:59,044
When a flood arose, the stream broke against
that house, and could not shake it, because

558
00:43:59,083 --> 00:44:00,583
it was founded on the rock.

559
00:44:01,623 --> 00:44:07,044
But he who hears and doesn’t do, is like a
man who built a house on the earth without

560
00:44:07,083 --> 00:44:13,724
a foundation, against which the stream broke,
and immediately it fell; and the ruin of

561
00:44:13,764 --> 00:44:15,063
that house was great.”

562
00:44:16,143 --> 00:44:19,083
Luke, chapter seven.

563
00:44:19,123 --> 00:44:24,804
After he had finished speaking in the
hearing of the people, he entered into Capernaum.

564
00:44:25,704 --> 00:44:31,924
A certain centurion’s servant, who was dear to
him, was sick and at the point of death.

565
00:44:32,524 --> 00:44:38,844
When he heard about Jesus, he sent to him
elders of the Jews, asking him to come and

566
00:44:38,884 --> 00:44:39,824
save his servant.

567
00:44:40,484 --> 00:44:46,804
When they came to Jesus, they begged him
earnestly, saying, “He is worthy for you to

568
00:44:46,844 --> 00:44:52,304
do this for him, for he loves our nation,
and he built our synagogue for us.”

569
00:44:53,204 --> 00:44:54,504
Jesus went with them.

570
00:44:54,544 --> 00:45:01,164
When he was now not far from the
house, the centurion sent friends to him, saying to

571
00:45:01,204 --> 00:45:07,724
him, “Lord, don’t trouble yourself, for I am
not worthy for you to come under my roof.

572
00:45:08,544 --> 00:45:14,504
Therefore I didn’t even think myself worthy to
come to you; but say the word, and my

573
00:45:14,544 --> 00:45:15,824
servant will be healed.

574
00:45:16,404 --> 00:45:21,524
For I also am a man placed under
authority, having under myself soldiers.

575
00:45:22,623 --> 00:45:24,204
I tell this one, ‘Go!’

576
00:45:24,984 --> 00:45:27,663
and he goes; and to another, ‘Come!’

577
00:45:28,324 --> 00:45:32,744
and he comes; and to my servant, ‘Do
this,’ and he does it.”

578
00:45:33,012 --> 00:45:38,852
When Jesus heard these things, he marvelled at
him, and turned and said to the multitude

579
00:45:38,892 --> 00:45:45,712
who followed him, “I tell you, I have not
found such great faith, no,

580
00:45:46,272 --> 00:45:47,172
not in Israel.”

581
00:45:47,652 --> 00:45:53,312
Those who were sent, returning to the house,
found that the servant who had been sick

582
00:45:53,352 --> 00:45:54,252
was well.

583
00:45:54,752 --> 00:45:58,032
Soon afterwards, he went to a city called
Nain.

584
00:45:58,972 --> 00:46:03,952
Many of his disciples, along with a great
multitude, went with him.

585
00:46:03,992 --> 00:46:10,692
Now when he came near to the gate of
the city, behold, one who was dead was carried out,

586
00:46:11,492 --> 00:46:14,872
the only born son of his mother, and she
was a widow.

587
00:46:15,972 --> 00:46:18,312
Many people of the city were with her.

588
00:46:18,992 --> 00:46:24,512
When the Lord saw her, he had compassion
on her and said to her, “Don’t cry.”

589
00:46:25,872 --> 00:46:29,952
He came near and touched the coffin, and
the bearers stood still.

590
00:46:30,912 --> 00:46:34,672
He said, “Young man, I tell you, arise!”

591
00:46:35,472 --> 00:46:38,292
He who was dead sat up and began to speak.

592
00:46:39,332 --> 00:46:40,972
Then he gave him to his mother.

593
00:46:41,652 --> 00:46:48,272
Fear took hold of all, and they glorified
God, saying, “A great prophet has arisen

594
00:46:48,312 --> 00:46:49,212
amongst us!”

595
00:46:49,752 --> 00:46:52,452
and, “God has visited his people!”

596
00:46:53,192 --> 00:46:58,752
This report went out concerning him in the
whole of Judea and in all the surrounding

597
00:46:58,792 --> 00:46:59,692
region.

598
00:47:00,372 --> 00:47:03,352
The disciples of John told him about all
these things.

599
00:47:04,252 --> 00:47:11,212
John, calling to himself two of his
disciples, sent them to Jesus, saying, “Are

600
00:47:11,252 --> 00:47:14,412
you the one who is coming, or should we
look for another?”

601
00:47:14,452 --> 00:47:21,352
When the men had come to him, they said,
“John the Baptiser has sent us to you, saying,

602
00:47:22,112 --> 00:47:27,812
‘Are you he who comes, or should we look
for another?’” In that hour he cured many of

603
00:47:27,852 --> 00:47:34,392
diseases and plagues and evil spirits; and
to many who were blind he gave sight.

604
00:47:35,272 --> 00:47:41,912
Jesus answered them, “Go and tell John the
things which you have seen and heard: that

605
00:47:41,952 --> 00:47:49,052
the blind receive their sight, the lame
walk, the lepers are cleansed, the deaf hear,

606
00:47:49,092 --> 00:47:53,332
the dead are raised up, and the poor have
good news preached to them.

607
00:47:53,912 --> 00:47:57,692
Blessed is he who finds no occasion for
stumbling in me.”

608
00:47:57,996 --> 00:48:04,736
When John’s messengers had departed, he began
to tell the multitudes about John, “What

609
00:48:04,776 --> 00:48:06,936
did you go out into the wilderness to see?

610
00:48:07,916 --> 00:48:09,556
A reed shaken by the wind?

611
00:48:10,516 --> 00:48:12,156
But what did you go out to see?

612
00:48:13,016 --> 00:48:15,096
A man clothed in soft clothing?

613
00:48:15,896 --> 00:48:22,076
Behold, those who are gorgeously dressed
and live delicately are in kings’ courts.

614
00:48:22,836 --> 00:48:24,776
But what did you go out to see?

615
00:48:25,516 --> 00:48:26,416
A prophet?

616
00:48:26,696 --> 00:48:30,136
Yes, I tell you, and much more than a
prophet.

617
00:48:31,156 --> 00:48:37,436
This is he of whom it is written, ‘Behold,
I send my messenger before your face, who

618
00:48:37,476 --> 00:48:39,316
will prepare your way before you.’

619
00:48:39,956 --> 00:48:45,716
“For I tell you, amongst those who are born
of women there is not a greater prophet than

620
00:48:45,756 --> 00:48:51,376
John the Baptiser; yet he who is least in
God’s Kingdom is greater than he.”

621
00:48:51,976 --> 00:48:57,416
When all the people and the tax collectors
heard this, they declared God to be just,

622
00:48:58,096 --> 00:49:00,476
having been baptised with John’s baptism.

623
00:49:01,756 --> 00:49:07,656
But the Pharisees and the lawyers rejected
the counsel of God, not being baptised by

624
00:49:07,696 --> 00:49:08,596
him themselves.

625
00:49:09,096 --> 00:49:11,876
“To what then should I compare the people
of this generation?

626
00:49:12,736 --> 00:49:13,636
What are they like?

627
00:49:14,536 --> 00:49:20,956
They are like children who sit in the
marketplace and call to one another, saying, ‘We

628
00:49:20,996 --> 00:49:23,216
piped to you, and you didn’t dance.

629
00:49:23,256 --> 00:49:25,956
We mourned, and you didn’t weep.’

630
00:49:27,096 --> 00:49:33,636
For John the Baptiser came neither eating bread
nor drinking wine, and you say, ‘He has

631
00:49:33,676 --> 00:49:34,576
a demon.’

632
00:49:34,756 --> 00:49:41,476
The Son of Man has come eating and drinking,
and you say, ‘Behold, a glutton and a drunkard,

633
