light.

1055
01:22:38,015 --> 01:22:40,055
The lamp of the body is the eye.

1056
01:22:40,915 --> 01:22:47,175
Therefore when your eye is good, your whole body
is also full of light; but when it is

1057
01:22:47,215 --> 01:22:50,355
evil, your body also is full of darkness.

1058
01:22:51,055 --> 01:22:54,415
Therefore see whether the light that is in
you isn’t darkness.

1059
01:22:55,675 --> 01:23:01,935
If therefore your whole body is full of
light, having no part dark, it will be wholly

1060
01:23:01,975 --> 01:23:06,575
full of light, as when the lamp with its
bright shining gives you light.”

1061
01:23:06,975 --> 01:23:17,535
Now as he spoke, a certain Pharisee

1062
01:23:17,575 --> 01:23:17,875
asked him to dine with him.

1063
01:23:17,915 --> 01:23:18,215
He went in and sat at the table.

1064
01:23:18,255 --> 01:23:20,415
When the Pharisee saw it, he marvelled that
he had not first washed himself before dinner.

1065
01:23:21,455 --> 01:23:27,775
The Lord said to him, “Now you Pharisees cleanse
the outside of the cup and of the platter,

1066
01:23:28,195 --> 01:23:31,915
but your inward part is full of extortion
and wickedness.

1067
01:23:32,715 --> 01:23:37,715
You foolish ones, didn’t he who made the
outside make the inside also?

1068
01:23:38,555 --> 01:23:44,715
But give for gifts to the needy those
things which are within, and behold, all things

1069
01:23:44,755 --> 01:23:46,015
will be clean to you.

1070
01:23:46,735 --> 01:23:48,615
But woe to you Pharisees!

1071
01:23:48,826 --> 01:23:55,466
For you tithe mint and rue and every herb,
but you bypass justice and God’s love.

1072
01:23:56,266 --> 01:24:00,406
You ought to have done these, and not to
have left the other undone.

1073
01:24:01,726 --> 01:24:03,226
Woe to you Pharisees!

1074
01:24:03,626 --> 01:24:08,686
For you love the best seats in
the synagogues and the greetings in the marketplaces.

1075
01:24:09,626 --> 01:24:12,806
Woe to you, scribes and Pharisees,
hypocrites!

1076
01:24:13,566 --> 01:24:18,606
For you are like hidden graves, and the
men who walk over them don’t know it.”

1077
01:24:18,906 --> 01:24:24,606
One of the lawyers answered him, “Teacher,
in saying this you insult us also.”

1078
01:24:25,606 --> 01:24:28,146
He said, “Woe to you lawyers also!

1079
01:24:28,966 --> 01:24:34,666
For you load men with burdens that are
difficult to carry, and you yourselves won’t even

1080
01:24:34,706 --> 01:24:37,426
lift one finger to help carry those
burdens.

1081
01:24:38,266 --> 01:24:39,226
Woe to you!

1082
01:24:39,966 --> 01:24:44,386
For you build the tombs of the prophets,
and your fathers killed them.

1083
01:24:45,186 --> 01:24:48,526
So you testify and consent to the works of
your fathers.

1084
01:24:49,226 --> 01:24:52,486
For they killed them, and you build their
tombs.

1085
01:24:53,186 --> 01:24:59,786
Therefore also the wisdom of God said, ‘I
will send to them prophets and apostles; and

1086
01:24:59,826 --> 01:25:05,546
some of them they will kill and persecute,
that the blood of all the prophets, which

1087
01:25:05,586 --> 01:25:11,566
was shed from the foundation of the world,
may be required of this generation, from the

1088
01:25:11,606 --> 01:25:16,926
blood of Abel to the blood of Zachariah,
who perished between the altar and the sanctuary.’

1089
01:25:17,766 --> 01:25:21,726
Yes, I tell you, it will be required of
this generation.

1090
01:25:23,006 --> 01:25:24,026
Woe to you lawyers!

1091
01:25:24,966 --> 01:25:27,026
For you took away the key of knowledge.

1092
01:25:27,806 --> 01:25:32,766
You didn’t enter in yourselves, and those
who were entering in, you hindered.”

1093
01:25:33,466 --> 01:25:39,006
As he said these things to them, the
scribes and the Pharisees began to be terribly angry,

1094
01:25:39,646 --> 01:25:45,206
and to draw many things out of him, lying
in wait for him, and seeking to catch him in

1095
01:25:45,246 --> 01:25:48,266
something he might say, that they might
accuse him.

1096
01:25:49,146 --> 01:25:51,306
Luke, chapter twelve.

1097
01:25:51,346 --> 01:25:57,946
Meanwhile, when a multitude of many thousands
had gathered together, so much so that

1098
01:25:57,986 --> 01:26:04,506
they trampled on each other, he began to
tell his disciples first of all, “Beware of

1099
01:26:04,546 --> 01:26:07,366
the yeast of the Pharisees, which is
hypocrisy.

1100
01:26:08,034 --> 01:26:14,054
But there is nothing covered up that will
not be revealed, nor hidden that will not be

1101
01:26:14,094 --> 01:26:14,994
known.

1102
01:26:15,254 --> 01:26:20,154
Therefore whatever you have said in the
darkness will be heard in the light.

1103
01:26:21,074 --> 01:26:26,734
What you have spoken in the ear in
the inner rooms will be proclaimed on the housetops.

1104
01:26:27,534 --> 01:26:34,154
“I tell you, my friends, don’t be afraid of
those who kill the body, and after that have

1105
01:26:34,194 --> 01:26:35,714
no more that they can do.

1106
01:26:36,774 --> 01:26:38,994
But I will warn you whom you should fear.

1107
01:26:39,454 --> 01:26:44,294
Fear him who after he has killed, has
power to cast into Gehenna.

1108
01:26:44,974 --> 01:26:47,634
Yes, I tell you, fear him.

1109
01:26:48,174 --> 01:26:51,374
“Aren’t five sparrows sold for two assaria
coins?

1110
01:26:52,054 --> 01:26:54,574
Not one of them is forgotten by God.

1111
01:26:55,514 --> 01:27:04,794
But the very hairs of your head are

1112
01:27:04,834 --> 01:27:05,134
all counted.

1113
01:27:05,174 --> 01:27:05,474
Therefore don’t be afraid.

1114
01:27:05,514 --> 01:27:05,814
You are of more value than many sparrows.

1115
01:27:05,854 --> 01:27:12,054
“I tell you, everyone who confesses me before
men, the Son of Man will also confess before

1116
01:27:12,094 --> 01:27:18,454
the angels of God; but he who denies me in
the presence of men will be denied in the

1117
01:27:18,494 --> 01:27:19,814
presence of God’s angels.

1118
01:27:20,694 --> 01:27:26,954
Everyone who speaks a word against the Son
of Man will be forgiven, but those who blaspheme

1119
01:27:26,994 --> 01:27:29,554
against the Holy Spirit will not be
forgiven.

1120
01:27:29,594 --> 01:27:35,594
When they bring you before the synagogues,
the rulers, and the authorities, don’t be

1121
01:27:35,634 --> 01:27:41,954
anxious how or what you will answer or what
you will say; for the Holy Spirit will teach

1122
01:27:41,994 --> 01:27:45,054
you in that same hour what you must say.”

1123
01:27:46,014 --> 01:27:52,334
One of the multitude said to him,
“Teacher, tell my brother to divide the inheritance

1124
01:27:52,374 --> 01:27:53,274
with me.”

1125
01:27:53,954 --> 01:27:59,794
But he said to him, “Man, who made me a
judge or an arbitrator over you?”

1126
01:28:00,534 --> 01:28:02,434
He said to them, “Beware!

1127
01:28:03,134 --> 01:28:09,014
Keep yourselves from covetousness, for a
man’s life doesn’t consist of the abundance

1128
01:28:09,054 --> 01:28:10,814
of the things which he possesses.”

1129
01:28:12,114 --> 01:28:17,974
He spoke a parable to them, saying, “The
ground of a certain rich man produced abundantly.

1130
01:28:19,114 --> 01:28:25,794
He reasoned within himself, saying, ‘What will I
do, because I don’t have room to store

1131
01:28:25,834 --> 01:28:26,734
my crops?’

1132
01:28:27,614 --> 01:28:30,074
He said, ‘This is what I will do.

1133
01:28:30,448 --> 01:28:37,028
I will pull down my barns, build bigger ones,
and there I will store all my grain and

1134
01:28:37,068 --> 01:28:37,968
my goods.

1135
01:28:38,388 --> 01:28:44,908
I will tell my soul, “Soul, you have many
goods laid up for many years.

1136
01:28:45,908 --> 01:28:53,148
Take your ease, eat, drink, and be merry.”’
“But God said to him, ‘You foolish one, tonight

1137
01:28:53,188 --> 01:28:55,368
your soul is required of you.

1138
01:28:55,408 --> 01:28:59,368
The things which you have prepared—whose
will they be?’

1139
01:29:00,288 --> 01:29:05,788
So is he who lays up treasure for himself,
and is not rich towards God.”

1140
01:29:06,928 --> 01:29:13,508
He said to his disciples, “Therefore I tell
you, don’t be anxious for your life, what

1141
01:29:13,548 --> 01:29:17,348
you will eat, nor yet for your body, what
you will wear.

1142
01:29:18,088 --> 01:29:21,768
Life is more than food, and the body is
more than clothing.

1143
01:29:22,908 --> 01:29:29,068
Consider the ravens: they don’t sow, they
don’t reap, they have no warehouse or barn,

1144
01:29:29,708 --> 01:29:30,988
and God feeds them.

1145
01:29:32,008 --> 01:29:34,328
How much more valuable are you than birds!

1146
01:29:34,848 --> 01:29:38,508
Which of you by being anxious can add a
cubit to his height?

1147
01:29:39,028 --> 01:29:44,968
If then you aren’t able to do even the
least things, why are you anxious about the rest?

1148
01:29:45,968 --> 01:29:48,388
Consider the lilies, how they grow.

1149
01:29:49,288 --> 01:29:56,068
They don’t toil, neither do they spin; yet
I tell you, even Solomon in all his glory

1150
01:29:56,108 --> 01:29:58,348
was not arrayed like one of these.

1151
01:29:59,068 --> 01:30:04,968
But if this is how God clothes the
grass in the field, which today exists and tomorrow

1152
01:30:05,008 --> 01:30:11,088
is cast into the oven, how much more will
he clothe you, O you of little faith?

1153
01:30:11,928 --> 01:30:16,648
“Don’t seek what you will eat or what you
will drink; neither be anxious.

1154
01:30:17,348 --> 01:30:23,168
For the nations of the world seek after
all of these things, but your Father knows that

1155
01:30:23,208 --> 01:30:24,368
you need these things.

1156
01:30:25,388 --> 01:30:29,888
But seek God’s Kingdom, and all these
things will be added to you.

1157
01:30:30,148 --> 01:30:35,448
“Don’t be afraid, little flock, for it is
your Father’s good pleasure to give you the

1158
01:30:35,488 --> 01:30:36,388
Kingdom.

1159
01:30:36,528 --> 01:30:39,688
Sell what you have and give gifts to the
needy.

1160
01:30:40,568 --> 01:30:46,268
Make for yourselves purses which don’t grow
old, a treasure in the heavens that doesn’t

1161
01:30:46,308 --> 01:30:50,728
fail, where no thief approaches and no
moth destroys.

1162
01:30:51,348 --> 01:30:54,808
For where your treasure is, there will
your heart be also.

1163
01:30:55,388 --> 01:30:58,288
“Let your waist be dressed and your lamps
burning.

1164
01:30:58,709 --> 01:31:04,789
Be like men watching for their lord when
he returns from the wedding feast, that when

1165
01:31:04,829 --> 01:31:08,769
he comes and knocks, they may immediately
open to him.

1166
01:31:09,709 --> 01:31:14,689
Blessed are those servants whom the lord
will find watching when he comes.

1167
01:31:15,629 --> 01:31:21,969
Most certainly I tell you that he will
dress himself, make them recline, and will come

1168
01:31:22,009 --> 01:31:22,909
and serve them.

1169
01:31:23,549 --> 01:31:29,049
They will be blessed if he comes in the
second or third watch and finds them so.

1170
01:31:29,749 --> 01:31:35,429
But know this, that if the master of the
house had known in what hour the thief was coming,

1171
01:31:36,329 --> 01:31:40,189
he would have watched and not allowed his
house to be broken into.

1172
01:31:41,109 --> 01:31:46,889
Therefore be ready also, for the Son of Man
is coming in an hour that you don’t expect

1173
01:31:46,929 --> 01:31:47,829
him.”

1174
01:31:47,929 --> 01:31:54,129
Peter said to him, “Lord, are you telling
this parable to us, or to everybody?”

1175
01:31:55,589 --> 01:32:01,709
The Lord said, “Who then is the faithful
and wise steward, whom his lord will set over

1176
01:32:01,749 --> 01:32:06,409
his household, to give them their portion
of food at the right times?

1177
01:32:07,289 --> 01:32:11,649
Blessed is that servant whom his lord will
find doing so when he comes.

1178
01:32:12,689 --> 01:32:17,109
Truly I tell you that he will set him over
all that he has.

1179
01:32:17,889 --> 01:32:24,069
But if that servant says in his heart,
‘My lord delays his coming,’ and begins to beat

1180
01:32:24,109 --> 01:32:30,489
the menservants and the maidservants, and to eat
and drink and to be drunken, then the

1181
01:32:30,529 --> 01:32:36,629
lord of that servant will come in a day
when he isn’t expecting him and in an hour that

1182
01:32:36,669 --> 01:32:42,789
he doesn’t know, and will cut him in two,
and place his portion with the unfaithful.

1183
01:32:43,069 --> 01:32:49,829
That servant who knew his lord’s will, and
didn’t prepare nor do what he wanted, will

1184
01:32:49,869 --> 01:32:56,109
be beaten with many stripes, but he who
didn’t know, and did things worthy of stripes,

1185
01:32:56,149 --> 01:32:58,529
will be beaten with few stripes.

1186
01:32:58,569 --> 01:33:04,989
To whomever much is given, of him will
much be required; and to whom much was entrusted,

1187
01:33:05,889 --> 01:33:07,429
of him more will be asked.

1188
01:33:08,569 --> 01:33:10,889
“I came to throw fire on the earth.

1189
01:33:11,609 --> 01:33:13,589
I wish it were already kindled.

1190
01:33:14,329 --> 01:33:20,249
But I have a baptism to be baptised with,
and how distressed I am until it is accomplished!

1191
01:33:20,872 --> 01:33:23,892
Do you think that I have come to give
peace in the earth?

1192
01:33:24,972 --> 01:33:27,972
I tell you, no, but rather division.

1193
01:33:29,172 --> 01:33:35,832
For from now on, there will be five in one
house divided, three against two, and

1194
01:33:35,872 --> 01:33:37,032
two against three.

1195
01:33:38,052 --> 01:33:44,832
They will be divided, father against son,
and son against father; mother against

1196
01:33:44,872 --> 01:33:51,272
daughter, and daughter against her mother;
mother-in-law against her daughter-in-law,

1197
01:33:51,312 --> 01:33:54,832
and daughter-in-law against her
mother-in-law.”

1198
01:33:54,872 --> 01:34:01,272
He said to the multitudes also, “When you
see a cloud rising from the west, immediately

1199
01:34:01,312 --> 01:34:05,392
you say, ‘A shower is coming,’ and so it
happens.

1200
01:34:05,432 --> 01:34:11,912
When a south wind blows, you say, ‘There
will be a scorching heat,’ and it

1201
01:34:11,952 --> 01:34:12,852
happens.

1202
01:34:13,452 --> 01:34:14,352
You hypocrites!

1203
01:34:14,892 --> 01:34:20,372
You know how to interpret the appearance of the
earth and the sky, but how is it that

1204
01:34:20,412 --> 01:34:21,972
you don’t interpret this time?

1205
01:34:22,912 --> 01:34:25,832
“Why don’t you judge for yourselves what
is right?

1206
01:34:26,432 --> 01:34:32,112
For when you are going with your
adversary before the magistrate, try diligently on the

1207
01:34:32,152 --> 01:34:38,312
way to be released from him, lest perhaps he
drag you to the judge, and the judge deliver

1208
01:34:38,352 --> 01:34:42,232
you to the officer, and the officer throw
you into prison.

1209
01:34:42,952 --> 01:34:48,972
I tell you, you will by no means get out
of there until you have paid the very last penny.”

1210
01:34:50,172 --> 01:34:52,972
Luke, chapter thirteen.

1211
01:34:53,012 --> 01:34:59,072
Now there were some present at the same
time who told him about the Galileans whose blood

1212
01:34:59,112 --> 01:35:01,252
Pilate had mixed with their sacrifices.

1213
01:35:02,192 --> 01:35:08,112
Jesus answered them, “Do you think that
these Galileans were worse sinners than all the

1214
01:35:08,152 --> 01:35:11,372
other Galileans, because they suffered
such things?

1215
01:35:11,972 --> 01:35:17,892
I tell you, no, but unless you repent, you
will all perish in the same way.

1216
01:35:18,492 --> 01:35:24,552
Or those eighteen on whom the tower in
Siloam fell and killed them—do you think that

1217
01:35:24,592 --> 01:35:27,792
they were worse offenders than all the men
who dwell in Jerusalem?

1218
01:35:28,792 --> 01:35:34,992
I tell you, no, but, unless you repent,
you will all perish in the same way.”

1219
01:35:35,972 --> 01:35:37,352
He spoke this parable.

1220
01:35:38,032 --> 01:35:43,772
“A certain man had a fig tree planted in
his vineyard, and he came seeking fruit on it

1221
01:35:43,812 --> 01:35:44,912
and found none.

1222
01:35:45,384 --> 01:35:51,684
He said to the vine dresser, ‘Behold, these
three years I have come looking for fruit

1223
01:35:51,724 --> 01:35:54,244
on this fig tree, and found none.

1224
01:35:55,084 --> 01:35:55,984
Cut it down!

1225
01:35:56,544 --> 01:35:58,164
Why does it waste the soil?’

1226
01:35:58,904 --> 01:36:05,484
He answered, ‘Lord, leave it alone this
year also, until I dig around it and

1227
01:36:05,524 --> 01:36:06,424
fertilise it.

1228
01:36:06,924 --> 01:36:14,084
If it bears fruit, fine; but if not, after
that, you can cut it down.’” He

1229
01:36:14,124 --> 01:36:17,104
was teaching in one of the synagogues on
the Sabbath day.

1230
01:36:18,044 --> 01:36:23,004
Behold, there was a woman who had a spirit
of infirmity eighteen years.

1231
01:36:23,624 --> 01:36:28,004
She was bent over and could in no way
straighten herself up.

1232
01:36:28,684 --> 01:36:35,484
When Jesus saw her, he called her and said
to her, “Woman, you are freed from your infirmity.”

1233
01:36:36,444 --> 01:36:41,804
He laid his hands on her, and immediately
she stood up straight and glorified God.

1234
01:36:42,484 --> 01:36:48,004
The ruler of the synagogue, being indignant
because Jesus had healed on the Sabbath,

1235
01:36:48,704 --> 01:36:53,524
said to the multitude, “There are six days
in which men ought to work.

1236
01:36:54,264 --> 01:36:58,984
Therefore come on those days and be
healed, and not on the Sabbath day!”

1237
01:36:59,404 --> 01:37:02,584
Therefore the Lord answered him, “You
hypocrites!

1238
01:37:03,064 --> 01:37:08,984
Doesn’t each one of you free his ox or
his donkey from the stall on the Sabbath and lead

1239
01:37:09,024 --> 01:37:10,044
him away to water?

1240
01:37:10,944 --> 01:37:16,444
Ought not this woman, being a daughter of
Abraham whom Satan had bound eighteen long

1241
01:37:16,484 --> 01:37:20,184
years, be freed from this bondage on the
Sabbath day?”

1242
01:37:20,844 --> 01:37:26,744
As he said these things, all his
adversaries were disappointed; and all the multitude

1243
01:37:26,784 --> 01:37:30,904
rejoiced for all the glorious things that
were done by him.

1244
01:37:31,964 --> 01:37:34,704
He said, “What is God’s Kingdom like?

1245
01:37:35,424 --> 01:37:36,984
To what shall I compare it?

1246
01:37:37,244 --> 01:37:41,984
It is like a grain of mustard seed which a
man took and put in his own garden.

1247
01:37:42,804 --> 01:37:47,984
It grew and became a large tree, and the
birds of the sky live in its branches.”

1248
01:37:49,264 --> 01:37:52,844
Again he said, “To what shall I compare
God’s Kingdom?

1249
01:37:53,764 --> 01:37:59,264
It is like yeast, which a woman took and
hid in three measures of flour, until it was

1250
01:37:59,304 --> 01:38:00,204
all leavened.”

1251
01:38:00,604 --> 01:38:06,164
He went on his way through cities
and villages, teaching, and travelling on to Jerusalem.

1252
01:38:07,484 --> 01:38:11,904
One said to him, “Lord, are they few who
are saved?”

1253
01:38:12,360 --> 01:38:18,860
He said to them, “Strive to enter in by
the narrow door, for many, I tell you,

1254
01:38:18,900 --> 01:38:22,940
will seek to enter in and will not be
able.

1255
01:38:22,980 --> 01:38:29,540
When once the master of the house has risen
up and has shut the door, and you begin to

1256
01:38:29,580 --> 01:38:36,240
stand outside and to knock at the door,
saying, ‘Lord, Lord, open to

1257
01:38:36,280 --> 01:38:37,080
us!’

1258
01:38:37,120 --> 01:38:42,200
then he will answer and tell you, ‘I don’t
know you or where you come from.’

1259
01:38:43,040 --> 01:38:49,100
Then you will begin to say, ‘We ate and
drank in your presence, and you taught in our

1260
01:38:49,140 --> 01:38:50,040
streets.’

1261
01:38:50,780 --> 01:38:55,080
He will say, ‘I tell you, I don’t know
where you come from.

1262
01:38:55,780 --> 01:38:58,900
Depart from me, all you workers of
iniquity.’

1263
01:38:59,360 --> 01:39:05,560
There will be weeping and gnashing of teeth
when you see Abraham, Isaac, Jacob, and all

1264
01:39:05,600 --> 01:39:09,600
the prophets in God’s Kingdom, and
yourselves being thrown outside.

1265
01:39:10,920 --> 01:39:16,980
They will come from the east, west, north,
and south, and will sit down in God’s Kingdom.

1266
01:39:17,780 --> 01:39:24,360
Behold, there are some who are last who will
be first, and there are some who are first

1267
01:39:24,780 --> 01:39:25,680
who will be last.”

1268
01:39:26,660 --> 01:39:33,220
On that same day, some Pharisees came,
saying to him, “Get out of here and go

1269
01:39:33,260 --> 01:39:36,420
away, for Herod wants to kill you.”

1270
01:39:36,460 --> 01:39:43,200
He said to them, “Go and tell that fox,
‘Behold, I cast out demons and perform

1271
01:39:43,240 --> 01:39:48,240
cures today and tomorrow, and the third
day I complete my mission.

1272
01:39:49,120 --> 01:39:55,720
Nevertheless I must go on my way today and
tomorrow and the next day, for it can’t be

1273
01:39:55,760 --> 01:39:58,200
that a prophet would perish outside of
Jerusalem.’

1274
01:39:58,900 --> 01:40:05,520
“Jerusalem, Jerusalem, you who kills the
prophets and stones those who are sent

1275
01:40:05,560 --> 01:40:06,460
to her!

1276
01:40:06,800 --> 01:40:12,880
How often I wanted to gather your children
together, like a hen gathers her own brood

1277
01:40:12,920 --> 01:40:15,380
under her wings, and you refused!

1278
01:40:16,120 --> 01:40:18,820
Behold, your house is left to you
desolate.

1279
01:40:19,680 --> 01:40:25,940
I tell you, you will not see me until you
say, ‘Blessed is he who comes in the name of

1280
01:40:25,980 --> 01:40:30,400
the Lord!’” Luke, chapter fourteen.

1281
01:40:30,440 --> 01:40:35,600
When he went into the house of one of
the rulers of the Pharisees on a Sabbath to eat

1282
01:40:35,640 --> 01:40:37,740
bread, they were watching him.

1283
01:40:38,400 --> 01:40:42,973
Behold, a certain man who had dropsy was
in front of him.

1284
01:40:43,013 --> 01:40:49,853
Jesus, answering, spoke to the lawyers and
Pharisees, saying, “Is it lawful to

1285
01:40:49,893 --> 01:40:50,893
heal on the Sabbath?”

1286
01:40:51,613 --> 01:40:52,733
But they were silent.

1287
01:40:53,933 --> 01:40:57,213
He took him, and healed him, and let him
go.

1288
01:40:57,693 --> 01:41:04,673
He answered them, “Which of you, if your
son or an ox fell into a well, wouldn’t

1289
01:41:04,713 --> 01:41:07,133
immediately pull him out on a Sabbath
day?”

1290
01:41:07,693 --> 01:41:09,913
They couldn’t answer him regarding these
things.

1291
01:41:10,733 --> 01:41:16,133
He spoke a parable to those who were
invited, when he noticed how they chose the best

1292
01:41:16,173 --> 01:41:23,153
seats, and said to them, “When you are
invited by anyone to a wedding feast, don’t

1293
01:41:23,193 --> 01:41:29,033
sit in the best seat, since perhaps
someone more honourable than you might be invited

1294
01:41:29,073 --> 01:41:35,573
by him, and he who invited both of you
would come and tell you, ‘Make room

1295
01:41:35,613 --> 01:41:36,673
for this person.’

1296
01:41:37,293 --> 01:41:41,653
Then you would begin, with shame, to take
the lowest place.

1297
01:41:42,253 --> 01:41:48,693
But when you are invited, go and sit in
the lowest place, so that when he who invited

1298
01:41:48,733 --> 01:41:53,293
you comes, he may tell you, ‘Friend, move
up higher.’

1299
01:41:54,413 --> 01:41:58,373
Then you will be honoured in the presence
of all who sit at the table with you.

1300
01:41:58,793 --> 01:42:04,693
For everyone who exalts himself will be
humbled, and whoever humbles himself will be

1301
01:42:04,733 --> 01:42:05,033
exalted.”

1302
01:42:05,073 --> 01:42:12,333
He also said to the one who had invited
him, “When you make a dinner or a supper, don’t

1303
01:42:12,373 --> 01:42:18,733
call your friends, nor your brothers, nor
your kinsmen, nor rich neighbours, or perhaps

1304
01:42:18,773 --> 01:42:22,153
they might also return the favour, and pay
you back.

1305
01:42:22,713 --> 01:42:29,353
But when you make a feast, ask the poor,
the maimed, the lame, or the blind; and

1306
01:42:29,393 --> 01:42:33,553
you will be blessed, because they don’t
have the resources to repay you.

1307
01:42:33,593 --> 01:42:37,173
For you will be repaid in the resurrection
of the righteous.”

1308
01:42:37,953 --> 01:42:44,293
When one of those who sat at the table
with him heard these things, he said to him, “Blessed

1309
01:42:44,333 --> 01:42:46,793
is he who will feast in God’s Kingdom!”

1310
01:42:47,853 --> 01:42:54,433
But he said to him, “A certain man made a
great supper, and he invited many people.

1311
01:42:55,073 --> 01:43:01,733
He sent out his servant at supper time
to tell those who were invited, ‘Come, for everything

1312
01:43:01,773 --> 01:43:02,773
is ready now.’

1313
01:43:03,973 --> 01:43:06,633
They all as one began to make excuses.

1314
01:43:07,201 --> 01:43:13,021
“The first said to him, ‘I have bought a
field, and I must go and see it.

1315
01:43:13,741 --> 01:43:15,541
Please have me excused.’

1316
01:43:16,341 --> 01:43:22,561
“Another said, ‘I have bought five yoke of
oxen, and I must go try them out.

1317
01:43:23,381 --> 01:43:24,981
Please have me excused.’

1318
01:43:25,581 --> 01:43:30,421
“Another said, ‘I have married a wife, and
therefore I can’t come.’

1319
01:43:31,061 --> 01:43:34,521
“That servant came, and told his lord
these things.

1320
01:43:35,221 --> 01:43:41,861
Then the master of the house, being angry,
said to his servant, ‘Go out quickly into

1321
01:43:41,901 --> 01:43:47,801
the streets and lanes of the city, and
bring in the poor, maimed, blind, and lame.’

1322
01:43:48,561 --> 01:43:54,021
“The servant said, ‘Lord, it is done as
you commanded, and there is still room.’

1323
01:43:55,041 --> 01:44:00,701
“The lord said to the servant, ‘Go out
into the highways and hedges, and compel them

1324
01:44:00,741 --> 01:44:03,261
to come in, that my house may be filled.

1325
01:44:03,301 --> 01:44:09,541
For I tell you that none of those men
who were invited will taste of my supper.’” Now

1326
01:44:09,581 --> 01:44:11,781
great multitudes were going with him.

1327
01:44:12,541 --> 01:44:18,881
He turned and said to them, “If anyone
comes to me, and doesn’t disregard his own father,

1328
01:44:19,421 --> 01:44:26,581
mother, wife, children, brothers, and
sisters, yes, and his own life also, he

1329
01:44:26,621 --> 01:44:27,641
can’t be my disciple.

1330
01:44:28,581 --> 01:44:33,661
Whoever doesn’t bear his own cross and
come after me, can’t be my disciple.

1331
01:44:34,841 --> 01:44:40,761
For which of you, desiring to build a
tower, doesn’t first sit down and count the cost,

1332
01:44:41,321 --> 01:44:43,441
to see if he has enough to complete it?

1333
01:44:43,841 --> 01:44:50,341
Or perhaps, when he has laid a foundation
and isn’t able to finish, everyone who

1334
01:44:50,381 --> 01:44:57,161
sees begins to mock him, saying, ‘This man
began to build and wasn’t able to finish.’

1335
01:44:57,541 --> 01:45:04,141
Or what king, as he goes to encounter another
king in war, will not sit down first and

1336
01:45:04,181 --> 01:45:10,021
consider whether he is able with ten thousand
to meet him who comes against him with

1337
01:45:10,061 --> 01:45:11,841
twenty thousand?

1338
01:45:11,881 --> 01:45:18,461
Or else, while the other is yet a great
way off, he sends an envoy and asks for conditions

1339
01:45:18,501 --> 01:45:19,401
of peace.

1340
01:45:19,881 --> 01:45:26,441
So therefore, whoever of you who doesn’t renounce
all that he has, he can’t be my disciple.

1341
01:45:27,841 --> 01:45:34,501
“Salt is good, but if the salt becomes
flat and tasteless, with what do you season it?

1342
01:45:34,725 --> 01:45:38,865
It is fit neither for the soil nor for the
manure pile.

1343
01:45:39,945 --> 01:45:40,905
It is thrown out.

1344
01:45:42,105 --> 01:45:45,525
He who has ears to hear, let him hear.”

1345
01:45:46,645 --> 01:45:49,725
Luke, chapter fifteen.

1346
01:45:49,765 --> 01:45:55,085
Now all the tax collectors and sinners
were coming close to him to hear him.

1347
01:45:55,645 --> 01:46:02,045
The Pharisees and the scribes murmured,
saying, “This man welcomes sinners, and eats

1348
01:46:02,085 --> 01:46:02,985
with them.”

1349
01:46:03,285 --> 01:46:10,045
He told them this parable: “Which of you men,
if you had one hundred sheep and lost one

1350
01:46:10,085 --> 01:46:15,705
of them, wouldn’t leave the ninety-nine in the
wilderness and go after the one that was

1351
01:46:15,745 --> 01:46:17,745
lost, until he found it?

1352
01:46:18,705 --> 01:46:23,065
When he has found it, he carries it on his
shoulders, rejoicing.

1353
01:46:23,805 --> 01:46:29,265
When he comes home, he calls together
his friends and his neighbours, saying to them,

1354
01:46:30,005 --> 01:46:34,365
‘Rejoice with me, for I have found my
sheep which was lost!’

1355
01:46:34,885 --> 01:46:40,325
I tell you that even so there will be more
joy in heaven over one sinner who repents,

1356
01:46:40,365 --> 01:46:45,025
than over ninety-nine righteous people who
need no repentance.

1357
01:46:45,805 --> 01:46:52,885
“Or what woman, if she had ten drachma
coins, if she lost one drachma coin, wouldn’t

1358
01:46:52,925 --> 01:46:58,285
light a lamp, sweep the house, and seek
diligently until she found it?

1359
01:46:58,725 --> 01:47:04,965
When she has found it, she calls
together her friends and neighbours, saying, ‘Rejoice

1360
01:47:05,005 --> 01:47:09,085
with me, for I have found the drachma
which I had lost!’

1361
01:47:10,025 --> 01:47:16,525
Even so, I tell you, there is joy in the
presence of the angels of God over

1362
01:47:16,565 --> 01:47:18,185
one sinner repenting.”

1363
01:47:18,445 --> 01:47:21,385
He said, “A certain man had two sons.

1364
01:47:22,265 --> 01:47:27,965
The younger of them said to his father,
‘Father, give me my share of your property.’

1365
01:47:28,885 --> 01:47:31,725
So he divided his livelihood between them.

1366
01:47:32,565 --> 01:47:38,885
Not many days after, the younger son
gathered all of this together and travelled into

1367
01:47:38,925 --> 01:47:39,865
a far country.

1368
01:47:40,825 --> 01:47:43,825
There he wasted his property with riotous
living.

1369
01:47:44,325 --> 01:47:50,745
When he had spent all of it, there arose
a severe famine in that country, and he began

1370
01:47:50,785 --> 01:47:51,745
to be in need.

1371
01:47:52,725 --> 01:47:58,745
He went and joined himself to one of the
citizens of that country, and he sent him into

1372
01:47:58,785 --> 01:48:00,565
his fields to feed pigs.

1373
01:48:01,345 --> 01:48:06,945
He wanted to fill his belly with the pods
that the pigs ate, but no one gave him any.

1374
01:48:07,217 --> 01:48:13,357
But when he came to himself, he said,
‘How many hired servants of my father’s have bread

1375
01:48:13,397 --> 01:48:16,537
enough to spare, and I’m dying with
hunger!

1376
01:48:17,457 --> 01:48:23,977
I will get up and go to my father,
and will tell him, “Father, I have sinned against

1377
01:48:24,017 --> 01:48:25,637
heaven and in your sight.

1378
01:48:26,417 --> 01:48:29,097
I am no more worthy to be called your son.

1379
01:48:29,597 --> 01:48:35,157
Make me as one of your hired servants.”’
“He arose and came to his father.

1380
01:48:36,037 --> 01:48:42,677
But while he was still far off, his father
saw him and was moved with compassion, and

1381
01:48:42,717 --> 01:48:45,997
ran, fell on his neck, and kissed him.

1382
01:48:47,117 --> 01:48:52,337
The son said to him, ‘Father, I have
sinned against heaven and in your sight.

1383
01:48:52,997 --> 01:48:55,477
I am no longer worthy to be called your
son.’

1384
01:48:56,257 --> 01:49:01,857
“But the father said to his servants, ‘Bring
out the best robe and put it on him.

1385
01:49:02,497 --> 01:49:05,597
Put a ring on his hand and sandals on his
feet.

1386
01:49:06,477 --> 01:49:13,197
Bring the fattened calf, kill it, and let’s
eat and celebrate; for this, my son, was

1387
01:49:13,237 --> 01:49:14,877
dead and is alive again.

1388
01:49:15,617 --> 01:49:17,257
He was lost and is found.’

1389
01:49:18,457 --> 01:49:19,857
Then they began to celebrate.

1390
01:49:20,897 --> 01:49:23,397
“Now his elder son was in the field.

1391
01:49:24,377 --> 01:49:27,757
As he came near to the house, he heard
music and dancing.

1392
01:49:28,637 --> 01:49:32,837
He called one of the servants to him and
asked what was going on.

1393
01:49:33,477 --> 01:49:38,957
He said to him, ‘Your brother has come,
and your father has killed the fattened calf,

1394
01:49:39,577 --> 01:49:42,437
because he has received him back safe and
healthy.’

1395
01:49:43,197 --> 01:49:45,797
But he was angry and would not go in.

1396
01:49:46,577 --> 01:49:49,317
Therefore his father came out and begged
him.

1397
01:49:49,657 --> 01:49:55,937
But he answered his father, ‘Behold, these
many years I have served you, and I never

1398
01:49:55,977 --> 01:50:01,797
disobeyed a commandment of yours, but you never
gave me a goat, that I might celebrate

1399
01:50:01,837 --> 01:50:02,977
with my friends.

1400
01:50:03,557 --> 01:50:09,597
But when this your son came, who
has devoured your living with prostitutes, you killed

1401
01:50:09,637 --> 01:50:11,457
the fattened calf for him.’

1402
01:50:12,297 --> 01:50:18,497
“He said to him, ‘Son, you are always with
me, and all that is mine is yours.

1403
01:50:19,197 --> 01:50:25,737
But it was appropriate to celebrate and be
glad, for this, your brother, was dead, and

1404
01:50:25,777 --> 01:50:26,677
is alive again.

1405
01:50:27,317 --> 01:50:31,677
He was lost, and is found.’” Luke, chapter
sixteen.

1406
01:50:32,807 --> 01:50:38,567
He also said to his disciples, “There was
a certain rich man who had a manager.

1407
01:50:39,587 --> 01:50:44,167
An accusation was made to him that this
man was wasting his possessions.

1408
01:50:45,367 --> 01:50:50,307
He called him, and said to him, ‘What is
this that I hear about you?

1409
01:50:51,227 --> 01:50:55,527
Give an accounting of your management, for
you can no longer be manager.’

1410
01:50:56,227 --> 01:51:02,587
“The manager said within himself, ‘What will I
do, seeing that my lord is taking away

1411
01:51:02,627 --> 01:51:04,607
the management position from me?

1412
01:51:05,527 --> 01:51:07,247
I don’t have strength to dig.

1413
01:51:07,967 --> 01:51:09,407
I am ashamed to beg.

1414
01:51:10,247 --> 01:51:16,227
I know what I will do, so that when
I am removed from management, they may receive me

1415
01:51:16,267 --> 01:51:17,167
into their houses.’

1416
01:51:17,647 --> 01:51:23,567
Calling each one of his lord’s debtors to him,
he said to the first, ‘How much do you

1417
01:51:23,607 --> 01:51:24,507
owe to my lord?’

1418
01:51:25,307 --> 01:51:27,907
He said, ‘A hundred batos of oil.’

1419
01:51:28,687 --> 01:51:33,467
He said to him, ‘Take your bill, and sit
down quickly and write fifty.’

1420
01:51:34,407 --> 01:51:37,567
Then he said to another, ‘How much do you
owe?’

1421
01:51:38,227 --> 01:51:40,727
He said, ‘A hundred cors of wheat.’

1422
01:51:41,507 --> 01:51:44,887
He said to him, ‘Take your bill, and write
eighty.’

1423
01:51:45,967 --> 01:51:52,067
“His lord commended the dishonest manager because
he had done wisely, for the children

1424
01:51:52,107 --> 01:51:57,407
of this world are, in their own
generation, wiser than the children of the light.

1425
01:51:57,887 --> 01:52:03,947
I tell you, make for yourselves friends by
means of unrighteous mammon, so that when

1426
01:52:03,987 --> 01:52:07,787
you fail, they may receive you into the
eternal tents.

1427
01:52:07,827 --> 01:52:12,047
He who is faithful in a very little is
faithful also in much.

1428
01:52:12,867 --> 01:52:17,327
He who is dishonest in a very little is
also dishonest in much.

1429
01:52:17,927 --> 01:52:23,247
If therefore you have not been faithful in
the unrighteous mammon, who will commit to

1430
01:52:23,287 --> 01:52:24,727
your trust the true riches?

1431
01:52:26,027 --> 01:52:30,987
If you have not been faithful in that
which is another’s, who will give you that which

1432
01:52:31,027 --> 01:52:31,927
is your own?

1433
01:52:32,287 --> 01:52:38,187
No servant can serve two masters, for either
he will hate the one and love the other;

1434
01:52:38,887 --> 01:52:42,367
or else he will hold to one and despise
the other.

1435
01:52:43,247 --> 01:52:45,707
You aren’t able to serve God and Mammon.”

1436
01:52:46,047 --> 01:52:52,287
The Pharisees, who were lovers of money,
also heard all these things, and they scoffed

1437
01:52:52,327 --> 01:52:52,797
at him.

1438
01:52:52,837 --> 01:52:59,477
He said to them, “You are those who justify
yourselves in the sight of men, but God knows

1439
01:52:59,517 --> 01:53:00,417
your hearts.

1440
01:53:01,117 --> 01:53:05,637
For that which is exalted amongst men is
an abomination in the sight of God.

1441
01:53:06,457 --> 01:53:09,257
“The law and the prophets were until John.

1442
01:53:10,177 --> 01:53:15,777
From that time the Good News of God’s
Kingdom is preached, and everyone is forcing his

1443
01:53:15,817 --> 01:53:16,757
way into it.

1444
01:53:17,237 --> 01:53:23,597
But it is easier for heaven and earth to
pass away than for one tiny stroke of a pen

1445
01:53:23,637 --> 01:53:24,777
in the law to fall.

1446
01:53:25,177 --> 01:53:29,477
“Everyone who divorces his wife and
marries another commits adultery.

1447
01:53:30,377 --> 01:53:34,437
He who marries one who is divorced from a
husband commits adultery.

1448
01:53:35,277 --> 01:53:41,777
“Now there was a certain rich man, and
he was clothed in purple and fine linen, living

1449
01:53:41,817 --> 01:53:43,217
in luxury every day.

1450
01:53:43,817 --> 01:53:50,617
A certain beggar, named Lazarus, was taken
to his gate, full of sores, and desiring

1451
01:53:50,657 --> 01:53:54,157
to be fed with the crumbs that fell from
the rich man’s table.

1452
01:53:55,157 --> 01:53:58,897
Yes, even the dogs came and licked his
sores.

1453
01:53:59,437 --> 01:54:04,497
The beggar died, and he was carried away
by the angels to Abraham’s bosom.

1454
01:54:05,037 --> 01:54:07,477
The rich man also died and was buried.

1455
01:54:08,417 --> 01:54:15,317
In Hades, he lifted up his eyes, being in
torment, and saw Abraham far off, and

1456
01:54:15,357 --> 01:54:16,797
Lazarus at his bosom.

1457
01:54:17,557 --> 01:54:24,057
He cried and said, ‘Father Abraham, have
mercy on me, and send Lazarus, that

1458
01:54:24,097 --> 01:54:27,977
he may dip the tip of his finger in water
and cool my tongue!

1459
01:54:28,657 --> 01:54:30,577
For I am in anguish in this flame.’

1460
01:54:31,877 --> 01:54:38,677
“But Abraham said, ‘Son, remember that you,
in your lifetime, received your good things,

1461
01:54:39,517 --> 01:54:42,177
and Lazarus, in the same way, bad things.

1462
01:54:42,897 --> 01:54:46,437
But here he is now comforted and you are
in anguish.

1463
01:54:47,037 --> 01:54:53,637
Besides all this, between us and you there
is a great gulf fixed, that those who want

1464
01:54:53,677 --> 01:54:59,757
to pass from here to you are not able, and
that no one may cross over from there to us.’

1465
01:55:00,177 --> 01:55:06,037
“He said, ‘I ask you therefore, father, that
you would send him to my father’s house—

1466
01:55:06,717 --> 01:55:13,037
for I have five brothers—that he may testify
to them, so they won’t also come into this

