02:43:29,724 --> 02:43:33,904
delivered him up to be condemned to death,
and crucified him.

2094
02:43:34,384 --> 02:43:37,324
But we were hoping that it was he who
would redeem Israel.

2095
02:43:37,840 --> 02:43:44,000
Yes, and besides all this, it is now the
third day since these things happened.

2096
02:43:45,660 --> 02:43:52,300
Also, certain women of our company amazed
us, having arrived early at the tomb; and

2097
02:43:52,340 --> 02:43:57,640
when they didn’t find his body, they came
saying that they had also seen a vision of

2098
02:43:57,680 --> 02:44:00,000
angels, who said that he was alive.

2099
02:44:00,780 --> 02:44:06,140
Some of us went to the tomb and found
it just like the women had said, but they didn’t

2100
02:44:06,180 --> 02:44:07,080
see him.”

2101
02:44:07,420 --> 02:44:13,460
He said to them, “Foolish people, and slow
of heart to believe in all that the prophets

2102
02:44:13,500 --> 02:44:14,400
have spoken!

2103
02:44:15,020 --> 02:44:19,040
Didn’t the Christ have to suffer these
things and to enter into his glory?”

2104
02:44:19,900 --> 02:44:24,840
Beginning from Moses and from all the prophets,
he explained to them in all the Scriptures

2105
02:44:24,880 --> 02:44:26,640
the things concerning himself.

2106
02:44:27,460 --> 02:44:32,680
They came near to the village where they were
going, and he acted like he would go further.

2107
02:44:33,340 --> 02:44:39,900
They urged him, saying, “Stay with us, for
it is almost evening, and the day is almost

2108
02:44:39,940 --> 02:44:40,840
over.”

2109
02:44:41,460 --> 02:44:43,180
He went in to stay with them.

2110
02:44:43,840 --> 02:44:48,440
When he had sat down at the table with
them, he took the bread and gave thanks.

2111
02:44:49,320 --> 02:44:51,240
Breaking it, he gave it to them.

2112
02:44:51,920 --> 02:44:57,300
Their eyes were opened and they recognised
him; then he vanished out of their sight.

2113
02:44:58,170 --> 02:45:03,520
They said to one another, “Weren’t our hearts
burning within us while he spoke to us

2114
02:45:03,560 --> 02:45:07,100
along the way, and while he opened the
Scriptures to us?”

2115
02:45:07,560 --> 02:45:14,040
They rose up that very hour, returned
to Jerusalem, and found the eleven gathered together,

2116
02:45:14,580 --> 02:45:20,640
and those who were with them, saying, “The
Lord is risen indeed, and has appeared to

2117
02:45:20,680 --> 02:45:21,580
Simon!”

2118
02:45:21,620 --> 02:45:27,100
They related the things that happened along the
way, and how he was recognised by them

2119
02:45:27,140 --> 02:45:28,420
in the breaking of the bread.

2120
02:45:29,280 --> 02:45:35,600
As they said these things, Jesus himself
stood amongst them, and said to them, “Peace

2121
02:45:35,640 --> 02:45:36,560
be to you.”

2122
02:45:37,100 --> 02:45:42,580
But they were terrified and filled with fear,
and supposed that they had seen a spirit.

2123
02:45:43,580 --> 02:45:46,280
He said to them, “Why are you troubled?

2124
02:45:47,240 --> 02:45:49,140
Why do doubts arise in your hearts?

2125
02:45:49,180 --> 02:45:53,360
See my hands and my feet, that it is truly
me.

2126
02:45:53,736 --> 02:46:00,316
Touch me and see, for a spirit doesn’t
have flesh and bones, as you see that

2127
02:46:00,357 --> 02:46:01,257
I have.”

2128
02:46:01,857 --> 02:46:05,997
When he had said this, he showed them his
hands and his feet.

2129
02:46:06,876 --> 02:46:13,476
While they still didn’t believe for joy, and
wondered, he said to them, “Do you have

2130
02:46:13,517 --> 02:46:14,736
anything here to eat?”

2131
02:46:15,337 --> 02:46:18,816
They gave him a piece of a broiled fish
and some honeycomb.

2132
02:46:19,696 --> 02:46:22,157
He took them, and ate in front of them.

2133
02:46:22,917 --> 02:46:28,996
He said to them, “This is what I told
you while I was still with you, that all things

2134
02:46:29,036 --> 02:46:35,456
which are written in the law of Moses,
the prophets, and the psalms concerning me must

2135
02:46:35,497 --> 02:46:36,396
be fulfilled.”

2136
02:46:37,077 --> 02:46:40,636
Then he opened their minds, that they
might understand the Scriptures.

2137
02:46:41,577 --> 02:46:47,496
He said to them, “Thus it is written, and
thus it was necessary for the Christ to suffer

2138
02:46:47,536 --> 02:46:53,676
and to rise from the dead the third
day, and that repentance and remission of sins should

2139
02:46:53,716 --> 02:46:57,917
be preached in his name to all the
nations, beginning at Jerusalem.

2140
02:46:59,097 --> 02:47:00,976
You are witnesses of these things.

2141
02:47:01,677 --> 02:47:05,517
Behold, I send out the promise of my
Father on you.

2142
02:47:06,236 --> 02:47:11,536
But wait in the city of Jerusalem until
you are clothed with power from on high.”

2143
02:47:12,036 --> 02:47:18,017
He led them out as far as Bethany, and he
lifted up his hands and blessed them.

2144
02:47:18,577 --> 02:47:23,216
While he blessed them, he withdrew from
them and was carried up into heaven.

2145
02:47:23,917 --> 02:47:30,176
They worshipped him and returned to Jerusalem
with great joy, and were continually in

2146
02:47:30,216 --> 02:47:32,997
the temple, praising and blessing God.

2147
02:47:33,857 --> 02:47:34,757
Amen.

2148
02:47:35,456 --> 02:47:37,216
Ecclesiastes, chapter one.

2149
02:47:37,257 --> 02:47:43,796
The words of the Preacher, the son of
David, king in Jerusalem: “Vanity of

2150
02:47:43,837 --> 02:47:48,937
vanities,” says the Preacher; “Vanity of
vanities, all is vanity.”

2151
02:47:50,097 --> 02:47:54,757
What does man gain from all his labour in
which he labours under the sun?

2152
02:47:55,657 --> 02:48:01,896
One generation goes, and another generation
comes; but the earth remains forever.

2153
02:48:02,577 --> 02:48:08,616
The sun also rises, and the sun goes down,
and hurries to its place where it rises.

2154
02:48:09,456 --> 02:48:13,277
The wind goes towards the south, and turns
around to the north.

2155
02:48:14,216 --> 02:48:19,736
It turns around continually as it goes,
and the wind returns again to its courses.

2156
02:48:20,356 --> 02:48:24,936
All the rivers run into the sea, yet the
sea is not full.

2157
02:48:26,016 --> 02:48:29,816
To the place where the rivers flow, there
they flow again.

2158
02:48:30,696 --> 02:48:34,336
All things are full of weariness beyond
uttering.

2159
02:48:35,236 --> 02:48:40,276
The eye is not satisfied with seeing, nor
the ear filled with hearing.

2160
02:48:41,016 --> 02:48:50,296
That which has been is that which

2161
02:48:50,336 --> 02:48:50,636
shall be, and that which has been done is
that which shall be done; and there is no new

2162
02:48:50,676 --> 02:48:51,596
thing under the sun.

2163
02:48:52,656 --> 02:48:57,116
Is there a thing of which it may be said,
“Behold, this is new?”

2164
02:48:57,496 --> 02:49:01,296
It has been long ago, in the ages which
were before us.

2165
02:49:01,876 --> 02:49:07,436
There is no memory of the former; neither
shall there be any memory of the latter that

2166
02:49:07,476 --> 02:49:10,816
are to come, amongst those that shall come
after.

2167
02:49:11,716 --> 02:49:15,796
I, the Preacher, was king over Israel in
Jerusalem.

2168
02:49:16,776 --> 02:49:23,236
I applied my heart to seek and to search
out by wisdom concerning all that is done under

2169
02:49:23,276 --> 02:49:24,176
the sky.

2170
02:49:24,456 --> 02:49:29,216
It is a heavy burden that God has given to
the sons of men to be afflicted with.

2171
02:49:29,996 --> 02:49:36,756
I have seen all the works that are done
under the sun; and behold, all is vanity and

2172
02:49:36,796 --> 02:49:38,056
a chasing after wind.

2173
02:49:38,956 --> 02:49:44,476
That which is crooked can’t be made straight;
and that which is lacking can’t be counted.

2174
02:49:45,336 --> 02:49:51,856
I said to myself, “Behold, I have obtained
for myself great wisdom above all who were

2175
02:49:51,896 --> 02:49:53,056
before me in Jerusalem.

2176
02:49:53,956 --> 02:49:58,436
Yes, my heart has had great experience of
wisdom and knowledge.”

2177
02:49:58,956 --> 02:50:03,096
I applied my heart to know wisdom, and to
know madness and folly.

2178
02:50:03,956 --> 02:50:07,556
I perceived that this also was a chasing
after wind.

2179
02:50:08,276 --> 02:50:14,596
For in much wisdom is much grief; and he
who increases knowledge increases sorrow.

2180
02:50:16,116 --> 02:50:18,376
Ecclesiastes, chapter two.

2181
02:50:18,416 --> 02:50:25,336
I said in my heart, “Come now, I will test
you with mirth; therefore enjoy pleasure;”

2182
02:50:26,316 --> 02:50:28,716
and behold, this also was vanity.

2183
02:50:29,916 --> 02:50:35,736
I said of laughter, “It is foolishness;”
and of mirth, “What does it accomplish?”

2184
02:50:36,321 --> 02:50:42,341
I searched in my heart how to cheer my
flesh with wine, my heart yet guiding me with

2185
02:50:42,381 --> 02:50:49,001
wisdom, and how to lay hold of folly, until
I might see what it was good for the sons

2186
02:50:49,041 --> 02:50:53,501
of men that they should do under heaven
all the days of their lives.

2187
02:50:54,081 --> 02:50:55,601
I made myself great works.

2188
02:50:56,201 --> 02:50:57,961
I built myself houses.

2189
02:50:58,821 --> 02:51:00,381
I planted myself vineyards.

2190
02:51:01,261 --> 02:51:07,241
I made myself gardens and parks, and I
planted trees in them of all kinds of fruit.

2191
02:51:08,421 --> 02:51:13,561
I made myself pools of water, to water the
forest where trees were grown.

2192
02:51:14,021 --> 02:51:19,221
I bought male servants and female servants,
and had servants born in my house.

2193
02:51:19,821 --> 02:51:25,561
I also had great possessions of herds and
flocks, above all who were before me in Jerusalem.

2194
02:51:26,681 --> 02:51:32,761
I also gathered silver and gold for myself,
and the treasure of kings and of the provinces.

2195
02:51:33,401 --> 02:51:39,821
I got myself male and female singers, and
the delights of the sons of men: musical instruments

2196
02:51:39,861 --> 02:51:40,881
of all sorts.

2197
02:51:41,721 --> 02:51:46,481
So I was great, and increased more than
all who were before me in Jerusalem.

2198
02:51:47,721 --> 02:51:49,941
My wisdom also remained with me.

2199
02:51:50,821 --> 02:51:54,261
Whatever my eyes desired, I didn’t keep
from them.

2200
02:51:54,621 --> 02:52:01,381
I didn’t withhold my heart from any joy,
for my heart rejoiced because of all my labour,

2201
02:52:01,421 --> 02:52:04,641
and this was my portion from all my
labour.

2202
02:52:04,681 --> 02:52:09,601
Then I looked at all the works that my
hands had worked, and at the labour that I had

2203
02:52:09,641 --> 02:52:16,341
laboured to do; and behold, all was vanity
and a chasing after wind, and

2204
02:52:16,381 --> 02:52:18,201
there was no profit under the sun.

2205
02:52:18,641 --> 02:52:24,521
I turned myself to consider wisdom, madness,
and folly; for what can the king’s successor

2206
02:52:24,561 --> 02:52:25,461
do?

2207
02:52:25,721 --> 02:52:28,021
Just that which has been done long ago.

2208
02:52:29,201 --> 02:52:34,481
Then I saw that wisdom excels folly, as
far as light excels darkness.

2209
02:52:35,501 --> 02:52:42,021
The wise man’s eyes are in his head,
and the fool walks in darkness—and yet I perceived

2210
02:52:42,061 --> 02:52:44,481
that one event happens to them all.

2211
02:52:45,021 --> 02:52:51,641
Then I said in my heart, “As it happens to
the fool, so will it happen even to me; and

2212
02:52:51,681 --> 02:52:53,381
why was I then more wise?”

2213
02:52:54,441 --> 02:52:57,341
Then I said in my heart that this also is
vanity.

2214
02:52:57,864 --> 02:53:04,604
For of the wise man, even as of the fool,
there is no memory forever, since

2215
02:53:04,644 --> 02:53:07,744
in the days to come all will have been
long forgotten.

2216
02:53:08,744 --> 02:53:12,744
Indeed, the wise man must die just like
the fool!

2217
02:53:13,224 --> 02:53:19,424
So I hated life, because the work that is
worked under the sun was grievous to me; for

2218
02:53:19,464 --> 02:53:22,384
all is vanity and a chasing after wind.

2219
02:53:22,424 --> 02:53:28,884
I hated all my labour in which I laboured
under the sun, because I must leave

2220
02:53:28,924 --> 02:53:30,984
it to the man who comes after me.

2221
02:53:31,984 --> 02:53:35,224
Who knows whether he will be a wise man or
a fool?

2222
02:53:35,864 --> 02:53:41,204
Yet he will have rule over all of my
labour in which I have laboured, and in which I

2223
02:53:41,244 --> 02:53:43,804
have shown myself wise under the sun.

2224
02:53:44,624 --> 02:53:46,264
This also is vanity.

2225
02:53:47,224 --> 02:53:52,804
Therefore I began to cause my heart to
despair concerning all the labour in which I had

2226
02:53:52,844 --> 02:53:53,984
laboured under the sun.

2227
02:53:54,584 --> 02:54:00,564
For there is a man whose labour
is with wisdom, with knowledge, and with skilfulness;

2228
02:54:00,604 --> 02:54:05,444
yet he shall leave it for his portion to a
man who has not laboured for it.

2229
02:54:06,264 --> 02:54:09,124
This also is vanity and a great evil.

2230
02:54:09,564 --> 02:54:15,204
For what does a man have of all his labour
and of the striving of his heart, in which

2231
02:54:15,244 --> 02:54:16,764
he labours under the sun?

2232
02:54:17,564 --> 02:54:24,104
For all his days are sorrows, and his
travail is grief; yes, even in the night

2233
02:54:24,144 --> 02:54:25,664
his heart takes no rest.

2234
02:54:26,544 --> 02:54:28,064
This also is vanity.

2235
02:54:28,744 --> 02:54:34,564
There is nothing better for a man than that
he should eat and drink, and make his soul

2236
02:54:34,604 --> 02:54:37,204
enjoy good in his labour.

2237
02:54:37,244 --> 02:54:41,164
This also I saw, that it is from the hand
of God.

2238
02:54:41,204 --> 02:54:45,604
For who can eat, or who can have
enjoyment, more than I?

2239
02:54:46,584 --> 02:54:53,004
For to the man who pleases him, God
gives wisdom, knowledge, and joy; but to the sinner

2240
02:54:53,044 --> 02:54:59,764
he gives travail, to gather and to heap up,
that he may give to him who pleases God.

2241
02:55:00,644 --> 02:55:04,244
This also is vanity and a chasing after
wind.

2242
02:55:06,024 --> 02:55:06,924
Ecclesiastes, chapter three.

2243
02:55:07,867 --> 02:55:14,367
For everything there is a season, and a
time for every purpose under heaven: a time

2244
02:55:14,407 --> 02:55:20,947
to be born, and a time to die; a time
to plant, and a time to pluck up that which is

2245
02:55:20,987 --> 02:55:27,467
planted; a time to kill, and a time to
heal; a time to break down, and a

2246
02:55:27,507 --> 02:55:34,107
time to build up; a time to weep, and a
time to laugh; a time to mourn, and a time

2247
02:55:34,147 --> 02:55:40,727
to dance; a time to cast away stones, and
a time to gather stones together; a

2248
02:55:40,767 --> 02:55:47,167
time to embrace, and a time to refrain from
embracing; a time to seek, and a time to

2249
02:55:47,207 --> 02:55:54,147
lose; a time to keep, and a time to cast
away; a time to tear, and a time to sew;

2250
02:55:54,187 --> 02:56:00,747
a time to keep silence, and a time to speak;
a time to love, and a time to hate; a

2251
02:56:00,787 --> 02:56:03,027
time for war, and a time for peace.

2252
02:56:04,027 --> 02:56:08,107
What profit has he who works in that in
which he labours?

2253
02:56:08,147 --> 02:56:13,187
I have seen the burden which God has given
to the sons of men to be afflicted with.

2254
02:56:13,667 --> 02:56:16,247
He has made everything beautiful in its
time.

2255
02:56:16,947 --> 02:56:23,547
He has also set eternity in their hearts, yet
so that man can’t find out the work that

2256
02:56:23,587 --> 02:56:26,467
God has done from the beginning even to
the end.

2257
02:56:27,507 --> 02:56:32,747
I know that there is nothing better for them
than to rejoice, and to do good as long

2258
02:56:32,787 --> 02:56:33,687
as they live.

2259
02:56:34,047 --> 02:56:40,147
Also that every man should eat and drink, and
enjoy good in all his labour, is the gift

2260
02:56:40,187 --> 02:56:41,087
of God.

2261
02:56:41,447 --> 02:56:44,787
I know that whatever God does, it shall be
forever.

2262
02:56:45,807 --> 02:56:51,647
Nothing can be added to it, nor anything taken
from it; and God has done it, that men

2263
02:56:51,687 --> 02:56:53,027
should fear before him.

2264
02:56:53,687 --> 02:56:59,107
That which is has been long ago, and that
which is to be has been long ago.

2265
02:57:00,007 --> 02:57:02,907
God seeks again that which is passed away.

2266
02:57:03,807 --> 02:57:10,547
Moreover I saw under the sun, in the place
of justice, that wickedness was there; and

2267
02:57:10,587 --> 02:57:13,787
in the place of righteousness, that
wickedness was there.

2268
02:57:14,607 --> 02:57:20,187
I said in my heart, “God will judge the
righteous and the wicked; for there is a time

2269
02:57:20,227 --> 02:57:23,027
there for every purpose and for every
work.”

2270
02:57:23,907 --> 02:57:30,527
I said in my heart, “As for the sons of
men, God tests them, so that they may see

2271
02:57:30,567 --> 02:57:32,527
that they themselves are like animals.

2272
02:57:33,046 --> 02:57:36,706
For that which happens to the sons of men
happens to animals.

2273
02:57:37,946 --> 02:57:39,866
Even one thing happens to them.

2274
02:57:40,486 --> 02:57:43,586
As the one dies, so the other dies.

2275
02:57:44,306 --> 02:57:51,546
Yes, they have all one breath; and man has
no advantage over the animals, for

2276
02:57:51,586 --> 02:57:52,486
all is vanity.

2277
02:57:52,886 --> 02:57:54,226
All go to one place.

2278
02:57:55,226 --> 02:57:58,646
All are from the dust, and all turn to
dust again.

2279
02:57:59,346 --> 02:58:05,866
Who knows the spirit of man, whether it
goes upward, and the spirit of the animal, whether

2280
02:58:05,906 --> 02:58:07,686
it goes downward to the earth?”

2281
02:58:08,806 --> 02:58:14,306
Therefore I saw that there is nothing better
than that a man should rejoice in his works,

2282
02:58:14,986 --> 02:58:20,286
for that is his portion; for who can bring
him to see what will be after him?

2283
02:58:20,886 --> 02:58:23,806
Ecclesiastes, chapter four.

2284
02:58:23,846 --> 02:58:29,186
Then I returned and saw all the oppressions
that are done under the sun: and behold,

2285
02:58:29,226 --> 02:58:35,446
the tears of those who were oppressed, and
they had no comforter; and on the side of

2286
02:58:35,486 --> 02:58:39,126
their oppressors there was power; but they
had no comforter.

2287
02:58:39,706 --> 02:58:45,266
Therefore I praised the dead who have been
long dead more than the living who are yet

2288
02:58:45,306 --> 02:58:46,206
alive.

2289
02:58:46,506 --> 02:58:53,186
Yes, better than them both is him who has
not yet been, who has not seen the evil

2290
02:58:53,226 --> 02:58:55,266
work that is done under the sun.

2291
02:58:55,746 --> 02:59:01,126
Then I saw all the labour and achievement
that is the envy of a man’s neighbour.

2292
02:59:01,166 --> 02:59:04,466
This also is vanity and a striving after
wind.

2293
02:59:05,426 --> 02:59:08,946
The fool folds his hands together and
ruins himself.

2294
02:59:10,266 --> 02:59:16,346
Better is a handful, with quietness, than
two handfuls with labour and chasing after

2295
02:59:16,386 --> 02:59:16,726
wind.

2296
02:59:16,766 --> 02:59:19,886
Then I returned and saw vanity under the
sun.

2297
02:59:20,846 --> 02:59:25,166
There is one who is alone, and he has
neither son nor brother.

2298
02:59:25,866 --> 02:59:31,246
There is no end to all of his
labour, neither are his eyes satisfied with wealth.

2299
02:59:32,306 --> 02:59:35,926
“For whom then do I labour and deprive my
soul of enjoyment?”

2300
02:59:37,146 --> 02:59:38,486
This also is vanity.

2301
02:59:39,466 --> 02:59:42,146
Yes, it is a miserable business.

2302
02:59:42,726 --> 02:59:47,406
Two are better than one, because they have
a good reward for their labour.

2303
02:59:47,446 --> 02:59:53,806
For if they fall, the one will lift up his
fellow; but woe to him who is alone when he

2304
02:59:53,846 --> 02:59:56,886
falls, and doesn’t have another to lift
him up.

2305
02:59:57,159 --> 03:00:03,739
Again, if two lie together, then they have
warmth; but how can one keep warm alone?

2306
03:00:04,599 --> 03:00:11,179
If a man prevails against one who is
alone, two shall withstand him; and

2307
03:00:11,219 --> 03:00:13,719
a threefold cord is not quickly broken.

2308
03:00:14,439 --> 03:00:20,399
Better is a poor and wise youth than an
old and foolish king who doesn’t know how to

2309
03:00:20,439 --> 03:00:23,319
receive admonition any more.

2310
03:00:23,359 --> 03:00:29,659
For out of prison he came out to be king;
yes, even in his kingdom he was born poor.

2311
03:00:30,299 --> 03:00:35,819
I saw all the living who walk under the
sun, that they were with the youth, the other,

2312
03:00:36,239 --> 03:00:37,279
who succeeded him.

2313
03:00:38,179 --> 03:00:44,679
There was no end of all the people, even
of all them over whom he was—yet those who

2314
03:00:44,719 --> 03:00:47,179
come after shall not rejoice in him.

2315
03:00:48,099 --> 03:00:51,839
Surely this also is vanity and a chasing
after wind.

2316
03:00:52,559 --> 03:00:55,539
Ecclesiastes, chapter five.

2317
03:00:55,579 --> 03:01:01,899
Guard your steps when you go to God’s house;
for to draw near to listen is better than

2318
03:01:01,939 --> 03:01:06,639
to give the sacrifice of fools, for they
don’t know that they do evil.

2319
03:01:07,779 --> 03:01:13,319
Don’t be rash with your mouth, and don’t
let your heart be hasty to utter anything before

2320
03:01:13,359 --> 03:01:16,939
God; for God is in heaven, and you on
earth.

2321
03:01:17,819 --> 03:01:19,719
Therefore let your words be few.

2322
03:01:20,699 --> 03:01:26,779
For as a dream comes with a multitude of
cares, so a fool’s speech with a multitude of

2323
03:01:26,819 --> 03:01:27,639
words.

2324
03:01:27,679 --> 03:01:33,599
When you vow a vow to God, don’t defer to
pay it; for he has no pleasure in fools.

2325
03:01:34,519 --> 03:01:35,739
Pay that which you vow.

2326
03:01:36,599 --> 03:01:41,599
It is better that you should not vow, than
that you should vow and not pay.

2327
03:01:42,659 --> 03:01:45,419
Don’t allow your mouth to lead you into
sin.

2328
03:01:46,339 --> 03:01:51,199
Don’t protest before the messenger that
this was a mistake.

2329
03:01:51,239 --> 03:01:56,179
Why should God be angry at your voice, and
destroy the work of your hands?

2330
03:01:56,819 --> 03:02:02,759
For in the multitude of dreams there are
vanities, as well as in many words; but you

2331
03:02:02,799 --> 03:02:03,879
must fear God.

2332
03:02:04,279 --> 03:02:09,959
If you see the oppression of the poor,
and the violent taking away of justice and righteousness

2333
03:02:09,999 --> 03:02:16,699
in a district, don’t marvel at the matter,
for one official is eyed by a higher one,

2334
03:02:16,739 --> 03:02:19,259
and there are officials over them.

2335
03:02:20,179 --> 03:02:22,819
Moreover the profit of the earth is for
all.

2336
03:02:23,539 --> 03:02:25,379
The king profits from the field.

2337
03:02:25,752 --> 03:02:32,912
He who loves silver shall not be satisfied
with silver, nor he who loves abundance, with

2338
03:02:32,952 --> 03:02:33,852
increase.

2339
03:02:34,412 --> 03:02:35,892
This also is vanity.

2340
03:02:37,072 --> 03:02:43,132
When goods increase, those who eat them
are increased; and what advantage is there to

2341
03:02:43,172 --> 03:02:46,472
its owner, except to feast on them with
his eyes?

2342
03:02:47,052 --> 03:02:53,492
The sleep of a labouring man is sweet,
whether he eats little or much; but the abundance

2343
03:02:53,532 --> 03:02:56,272
of the rich will not allow him to sleep.

2344
03:02:57,292 --> 03:03:03,312
There is a grievous evil which I have seen
under the sun: wealth kept by its owner to

2345
03:03:03,352 --> 03:03:04,252
his harm.

2346
03:03:04,472 --> 03:03:10,532
Those riches perish by misfortune, and if
he has fathered a son, there is nothing in

2347
03:03:10,572 --> 03:03:11,472
his hand.

2348
03:03:11,952 --> 03:03:18,192
As he came out of his mother’s womb, naked
shall he go again as he came, and shall take

2349
03:03:18,232 --> 03:03:22,052
nothing for his labour, which he may carry
away in his hand.

2350
03:03:22,672 --> 03:03:28,792
This also is a grievous evil, that in all
points as he came, so shall he go.

2351
03:03:29,332 --> 03:03:32,712
And what profit does he have who labours
for the wind?

2352
03:03:33,692 --> 03:03:39,992
All his days he also eats in darkness, he
is frustrated, and has sickness and wrath.

2353
03:03:40,612 --> 03:03:46,572
Behold, that which I have seen to be good
and proper is for one to eat and to drink,

2354
03:03:47,152 --> 03:03:53,052
and to enjoy good in all his labour, in
which he labours under the sun, all the days

2355
03:03:53,092 --> 03:03:57,092
of his life which God has given him; for
this is his portion.

2356
03:03:57,752 --> 03:04:03,972
Every man also to whom God has given riches
and wealth, and has given him power to eat

2357
03:04:04,012 --> 03:04:10,492
of it, and to take his portion, and to
rejoice in his labour—this is the gift of God.

2358
03:04:10,952 --> 03:04:16,592
For he shall not often reflect on the days
of his life, because God occupies him with

2359
03:04:16,632 --> 03:04:17,752
the joy of his heart.

2360
03:04:18,312 --> 03:04:21,912
Ecclesiastes, chapter six.

2361
03:04:21,952 --> 03:04:28,232
There is an evil which I have seen under the
sun, and it is heavy on men: a man to whom

2362
03:04:28,272 --> 03:04:34,272
God gives riches, wealth, and honour, so that
he lacks nothing for his soul of all that

2363
03:04:34,312 --> 03:04:40,172
he desires, yet God gives him no power to
eat of it, but an alien eats it.

2364
03:04:40,652 --> 03:04:43,472
This is vanity, and it is an evil disease.

2365
03:04:44,112 --> 03:04:50,712
If a man fathers a hundred children, and lives
many years, so that the days of his years

2366
03:04:50,752 --> 03:04:58,352
are many, but his soul is not filled with
good, and moreover he has no burial, I

2367
03:04:58,392 --> 03:05:04,812
say that a stillborn child is better than
he; for it comes in vanity, and departs in

2368
03:05:04,852 --> 03:05:08,252
darkness, and its name is covered with
darkness.

2369
03:05:09,252 --> 03:05:12,752
Moreover it has not seen the sun nor known
it.

2370
03:05:13,752 --> 03:05:15,852
This has rest rather than the other.

2371
03:05:16,212 --> 03:05:23,872
Yes, though he live a thousand years twice
told, and yet fails to enjoy good, don’t

2372
03:05:23,912 --> 03:05:25,152
all go to one place?

2373
03:05:25,832 --> 03:05:30,672
All the labour of man is for his mouth,
and yet the appetite is not filled.

2374
03:05:31,412 --> 03:05:34,712
For what advantage has the wise more than
the fool?

2375
03:05:35,812 --> 03:05:39,692
What has the poor man, that knows how to
walk before the living?

2376
03:05:39,732 --> 03:05:43,752
Better is the sight of the eyes than the
wandering of the desire.

2377
03:05:44,572 --> 03:05:47,832
This also is vanity and a chasing after
wind.

2378
03:05:48,772 --> 03:05:55,412
Whatever has been, its name was given long
ago; and it is known what man is;

2379
03:05:56,272 --> 03:05:59,792
neither can he contend with him who is
mightier than he.

2380
03:06:00,192 --> 03:06:02,532
For there are many words that create
vanity.

2381
03:06:03,632 --> 03:06:05,272
What does that profit man?

2382
03:06:05,852 --> 03:06:12,052
For who knows what is good for man in life,
all the days of his vain life which he spends

2383
03:06:12,092 --> 03:06:13,032
like a shadow?

2384
03:06:13,592 --> 03:06:17,892
For who can tell a man what will be after
him under the sun?

2385
03:06:26,892 --> 03:06:27,412
Ecclesiastes, chapter seven.

2386
03:06:27,452 --> 03:06:27,752
A good name is better than fine perfume; and
the day of death better than the day of

2387
03:06:27,792 --> 03:06:28,692
one’s birth.

2388
03:06:28,892 --> 03:06:34,812
It is better to go to the house of
mourning than to go to the house of feasting; for

2389
03:06:34,852 --> 03:06:39,072
that is the end of all men, and the living
should take this to heart.

2390
03:06:39,552 --> 03:06:45,332
Sorrow is better than laughter; for by the
sadness of the face the heart is made good.

2391
03:06:46,352 --> 03:06:51,712
The heart of the wise is in the house of
mourning; but the heart of fools is in the house

2392
03:06:51,752 --> 03:06:52,652
of mirth.

2393
03:06:53,412 --> 03:06:58,712
It is better to hear the rebuke of the wise
than for a man to hear the song of fools.

2394
03:06:59,832 --> 03:07:04,852
For as the crackling of thorns under a
pot, so is the laughter of the fool.

2395
03:07:05,892 --> 03:07:07,312
This also is vanity.

2396
03:07:07,815 --> 03:07:13,935
Surely extortion makes the wise man
foolish; and a bribe destroys the understanding.

2397
03:07:15,035 --> 03:07:17,775
Better is the end of a thing than its
beginning.

2398
03:07:19,135 --> 03:07:22,495
The patient in spirit is better than the
proud in spirit.

2399
03:07:23,055 --> 03:07:28,475
Don’t be hasty in your spirit to be angry,
for anger rests in the bosom of fools.

2400
03:07:29,435 --> 03:07:33,095
Don’t say, “Why were the former days
better than these?”

2401
03:07:34,095 --> 03:07:36,355
For you do not ask wisely about this.

2402
03:07:37,155 --> 03:07:39,415
Wisdom is as good as an inheritance.

2403
03:07:40,315 --> 03:07:43,895
Yes, it is more excellent for those who
see the sun.

2404
03:07:44,555 --> 03:07:50,475
For wisdom is a defence, even as money is
a defence; but the excellency of knowledge

2405
03:07:50,515 --> 03:07:53,995
is that wisdom preserves the life of him
who has it.

2406
03:07:54,975 --> 03:08:00,055
Consider the work of God, for who can make
that straight which he has made crooked?

2407
03:08:00,095 --> 03:08:06,895
In the day of prosperity be joyful, and in
the day of adversity consider; yes,

2408
03:08:07,595 --> 03:08:13,875
God has made the one side by side with the
other, to the end that man should not find

2409
03:08:13,915 --> 03:08:15,435
out anything after him.

2410
03:08:16,355 --> 03:08:22,935
All this I have seen in my days of
vanity: there is a righteous man who perishes in his

2411
03:08:22,975 --> 03:08:27,615
righteousness, and there is a wicked man
who lives long in his evildoing.

2412
03:08:27,655 --> 03:08:32,575
Don’t be overly righteous, neither make
yourself overly wise.

2413
03:08:33,575 --> 03:08:35,075
Why should you destroy yourself?

2414
03:08:36,115 --> 03:08:38,715
Don’t be too wicked, neither be foolish.

2415
03:08:39,215 --> 03:08:41,255
Why should you die before your time?

2416
03:08:42,055 --> 03:08:44,475
It is good that you should take hold of
this.

2417
03:08:45,215 --> 03:08:51,715
Yes, also don’t withdraw your hand from that;
for he who fears God will come out of

2418
03:08:51,755 --> 03:08:52,655
them all.

2419
03:08:53,155 --> 03:08:58,335
Wisdom is a strength to the wise man more
than ten rulers who are in a city.

2420
03:08:59,355 --> 03:09:04,095
Surely there is not a righteous man on
earth who does good and doesn’t sin.

2421
03:09:04,595 --> 03:09:10,415
Also don’t take heed to all words that
are spoken, lest you hear your servant curse you;

2422
03:09:10,935 --> 03:09:15,515
for often your own heart knows that you
yourself have likewise cursed others.

2423
03:09:16,475 --> 03:09:18,515
All this I have proved in wisdom.

2424
03:09:18,555 --> 03:09:23,675
I said, “I will be wise;” but it was far
from me.

2425
03:09:24,435 --> 03:09:28,315
That which is, is far off and exceedingly
deep.

2426
03:09:28,875 --> 03:09:29,975
Who can find it out?

2427
03:09:30,307 --> 03:09:36,907
I turned around, and my heart sought to know
and to search out, and to seek wisdom and

2428
03:09:36,947 --> 03:09:42,847
the scheme of things, and to know
that wickedness is stupidity, and that foolishness

2429
03:09:42,887 --> 03:09:43,787
is madness.

2430
03:09:44,527 --> 03:09:50,827
I find more bitter than death the woman
whose heart is snares and traps, whose hands

2431
03:09:50,867 --> 03:09:51,767
are chains.

2432
03:09:52,227 --> 03:09:57,667
Whoever pleases God shall escape from her;
but the sinner will be ensnared by her.

2433
03:09:58,467 --> 03:10:05,147
“Behold, I have found this,” says the
Preacher, “to one another, to find an explanation

2434
03:10:05,187 --> 03:10:09,147
which my soul still seeks, but I have not
found.

2435
03:10:09,667 --> 03:10:15,367
I have found one man amongst a thousand, but
I have not found a woman amongst all those.

2436
03:10:16,327 --> 03:10:22,807
Behold, I have only found this: that God
made mankind upright; but they search

2437
03:10:22,847 --> 03:10:24,107
for many inventions.”

2438
03:10:24,647 --> 03:10:27,627
Ecclesiastes, chapter eight.

2439
03:10:27,667 --> 03:10:29,127
Who is like the wise man?

2440
03:10:29,727 --> 03:10:32,207
And who knows the interpretation of a
thing?

2441
03:10:32,887 --> 03:10:38,187
A man’s wisdom makes his face shine, and
the hardness of his face is changed.

2442
03:10:39,547 --> 03:10:41,727
I say, “Keep the king’s command!”

2443
03:10:42,567 --> 03:10:43,927
because of the oath to God.

2444
03:10:44,427 --> 03:10:46,567
Don’t be hasty to go out of his presence.

2445
03:10:47,387 --> 03:10:53,227
Don’t persist in an evil thing, for he
does whatever pleases him, for the king’s word

2446
03:10:53,267 --> 03:10:54,167
is supreme.

2447
03:10:54,547 --> 03:10:57,087
Who can say to him, “What are you doing?”

2448
03:10:58,127 --> 03:11:03,647
Whoever keeps the commandment shall not come to
harm, and his wise heart will know the

2449
03:11:03,687 --> 03:11:04,587
time and procedure.

2450
03:11:05,667 --> 03:11:11,287
For there is a time and procedure for
every purpose, although the misery of man is heavy

2451
03:11:11,327 --> 03:11:12,227
on him.

2452
03:11:12,487 --> 03:11:16,987
For he doesn’t know that which will be;
for who can tell him how it will be?

2453
03:11:17,887 --> 03:11:24,227
There is no man who has power over
the spirit to contain the spirit; neither does he

2454
03:11:24,267 --> 03:11:26,147
have power over the day of death.

2455
03:11:27,107 --> 03:11:32,727
There is no discharge in war; neither
shall wickedness deliver those who practise it.

2456
03:11:33,087 --> 03:11:39,447
All this I have seen, and applied my mind
to every work that is done under the sun.

2457
03:11:40,347 --> 03:11:44,927
There is a time in which one man has power
over another to his hurt.

2458
03:11:45,267 --> 03:11:46,687
So I saw the wicked buried.

2459
03:11:47,667 --> 03:11:49,827
Indeed they came also from holiness.

2460
03:11:49,867 --> 03:11:53,907
They went and were forgotten in the city
where they did this.

2461
03:11:54,407 --> 03:11:55,567
This also is vanity.

2462
03:11:56,079 --> 03:12:02,499
Because sentence against an evil work is
not executed speedily, therefore the heart of

2463
03:12:02,539 --> 03:12:05,979
the sons of men is fully set in them to do
evil.

2464
03:12:06,979 --> 03:12:13,879
Though a sinner commits crimes a hundred times,
and lives long, yet surely I know that

2465
03:12:13,919 --> 03:12:18,539
it will be better with those who fear God,
who are reverent before him.

2466
03:12:19,199 --> 03:12:24,599
But it shall not be well with the
wicked, neither shall he lengthen days like a shadow,

2467
03:12:25,339 --> 03:12:26,939
because he doesn’t fear God.

2468
03:12:27,879 --> 03:12:33,199
There is a vanity which is done on the
earth, that there are righteous men to whom it

2469
03:12:33,239 --> 03:12:35,439
happens according to the work of the
wicked.

2470
03:12:36,079 --> 03:12:40,979
Again, there are wicked men to whom it
happens according to the work of the righteous.

2471
03:12:42,279 --> 03:12:44,219
I said that this also is vanity.

2472
03:12:45,019 --> 03:12:50,919
Then I commended mirth, because a man has
no better thing under the sun than to eat,

2473
03:12:51,439 --> 03:12:57,979
to drink, and to be joyful: for that will
accompany him in his labour all the days of

2474
03:12:58,019 --> 03:13:00,679
his life which God has given him under the
sun.

2475
03:13:01,359 --> 03:13:06,699
When I applied my heart to know wisdom, and
to see the business that is done on the earth

2476
03:13:07,359 --> 03:13:14,199
(even though eyes see no sleep day or night),
then I saw all the work of God, that

2477
03:13:14,239 --> 03:13:19,919
man can’t find out the work that is done
under the sun, because however much a man labours

2478
03:13:19,959 --> 03:13:22,599
to seek it out, yet he won’t find it.

2479
03:13:23,059 --> 03:13:28,799
Yes even though a wise man thinks he can
comprehend it, he won’t be able to find it.

2480
03:13:30,579 --> 03:13:32,399
Ecclesiastes, chapter nine.

2481
03:13:32,439 --> 03:13:39,179
For all this I laid to my heart, even to
explore all this: that the righteous, and

2482
03:13:39,219 --> 03:13:45,919
the wise, and their works, are in the hand
of God; whether it is love or hatred, man

2483
03:13:45,959 --> 03:13:48,619
doesn’t know it; all is before them.

2484
03:13:49,139 --> 03:13:51,359
All things come alike to all.

2485
03:13:52,259 --> 03:13:58,299
There is one event to the righteous and to
the wicked; to the good, to the clean, to

2486
03:13:58,339 --> 03:14:03,159
the unclean, to him who sacrifices, and to
him who doesn’t sacrifice.

2487
03:14:04,559 --> 03:14:11,059
As is the good, so is the sinner; he who
takes an oath, as he who fears an

2488
03:14:11,099 --> 03:14:11,999
oath.

2489
03:14:12,579 --> 03:14:18,819
This is an evil in all that is done under
the sun, that there is one event to all.

2490
03:14:19,116 --> 03:14:25,796
Yes also, the heart of the sons of men
is full of evil, and madness is in their heart

2491
03:14:25,836 --> 03:14:29,596
while they live, and after that they go to
the dead.

2492
03:14:30,736 --> 03:14:36,596
For to him who is joined with all the
living there is hope; for a living dog is better

2493
03:14:36,636 --> 03:14:37,536
than a dead lion.

2494
03:14:38,296 --> 03:14:44,036
For the living know that they will die,
but the dead don’t know anything, neither do

2495
03:14:44,076 --> 03:14:47,936
they have any more a reward; for their
memory is forgotten.

2496
03:14:49,116 --> 03:14:55,456
Also their love, their hatred, and their
envy has perished long ago; neither do they

2497
03:14:55,496 --> 03:15:00,336
any longer have a portion forever in
anything that is done under the sun.

2498
03:15:01,216 --> 03:15:07,856
Go your way—eat your bread with joy, and
drink your wine with a merry heart; for

2499
03:15:07,896 --> 03:15:10,156
God has already accepted your works.

2500
03:15:11,196 --> 03:15:15,636
Let your garments be always white, and
don’t let your head lack oil.

2501
03:15:16,396 --> 03:15:22,256
Live joyfully with the wife whom you love
all the days of your life of vanity, which

2502
03:15:22,296 --> 03:15:28,516
he has given you under the sun, all your
days of vanity, for that is your portion in

2503
03:15:28,556 --> 03:15:32,196
life, and in your labour in which you
labour under the sun.

2504
03:15:32,556 --> 03:15:38,796
Whatever your hand finds to do, do it with
your might; for there is no work, nor plan,

2505
03:15:39,336 --> 03:15:42,996
nor knowledge, nor wisdom, in Sheol, where
you are going.

2506
03:15:43,856 --> 03:15:50,376
I returned and saw under the sun that the
race is not to the swift, nor the battle

2507
03:15:50,416 --> 03:15:56,276
to the strong, neither yet bread to the
wise, nor yet riches to men of understanding,

2508
03:15:57,356 --> 03:16:02,296
nor yet favour to men of skill; but time
and chance happen to them all.

2509
03:16:03,136 --> 03:16:05,476
For man also doesn’t know his time.

2510
03:16:06,316 --> 03:16:12,146
As the fish that are taken in an evil net,
and as the birds that are caught in the snare,

2511
03:16:12,706 --> 03:16:19,186
even so are the sons of men snared in an
evil time, when it falls suddenly on them.

2512
03:16:19,726 --> 03:16:25,166
I have also seen wisdom under the sun in
this way, and it seemed great to me.

2513
03:16:26,026 --> 03:16:32,486
There was a little city, and few men within
it; and a great king came against it, besieged

2514
03:16:32,526 --> 03:16:35,706
it, and built great bulwarks against it.

2515
03:16:35,986 --> 03:16:42,446
Now a poor wise man was found in it, and
he by his wisdom delivered the city; yet

2516
03:16:42,486 --> 03:16:45,066
no man remembered that same poor man.

2517
03:16:45,433 --> 03:16:48,793
Then I said, “Wisdom is better than
strength.”

2518
03:16:50,033 --> 03:16:55,533
Nevertheless the poor man’s wisdom is
despised, and his words are not heard.

2519
03:16:56,713 --> 03:17:01,993
The words of the wise heard in quiet are
better than the cry of him who rules amongst

2520
03:17:02,033 --> 03:17:02,933
fools.

2521
03:17:03,833 --> 03:17:09,393
Wisdom is better than weapons of war; but
one sinner destroys much good.

2522
03:17:09,933 --> 03:17:12,973
Ecclesiastes, chapter ten.

2523
03:17:13,013 --> 03:17:19,793
Dead flies cause the oil of the perfumer to
produce an evil odour; so does a little folly

2524
03:17:19,833 --> 03:17:22,713
outweigh wisdom and honour.

2525
03:17:22,753 --> 03:17:27,733
A wise man’s heart is at his right hand,
but a fool’s heart at his left.

2526
03:17:28,413 --> 03:17:34,953
Yes also when the fool walks by the
way, his understanding fails him, and he says to

2527
03:17:34,993 --> 03:17:36,613
everyone that he is a fool.

2528
03:17:37,833 --> 03:17:43,913
If the spirit of the ruler rises up
against you, don’t leave your place; for gentleness

2529
03:17:43,953 --> 03:17:45,853
lays great offences to rest.

2530
03:17:46,593 --> 03:17:52,353
There is an evil which I have seen under
the sun, the sort of error which proceeds from

2531
03:17:52,393 --> 03:17:53,293
the ruler.

2532
03:17:53,953 --> 03:18:02,453
Folly is set in

2533
03:18:02,493 --> 03:18:02,793
great dignity, and the rich sit in a low
place.

2534
03:18:02,833 --> 03:18:04,993
I have seen servants on horses, and
princes walking like servants on the earth.

2535
03:18:05,893 --> 03:18:11,633
He who digs a pit may fall into it;
and whoever breaks through a wall may be bitten by

2536
03:18:11,673 --> 03:18:12,573
a snake.

2537
03:18:13,013 --> 03:18:16,173
Whoever carves out stones may be injured
by them.

2538
03:18:16,773 --> 03:18:19,853
Whoever splits wood may be endangered by
it.

2539
03:18:20,573 --> 03:18:26,193
If the axe is blunt, and one doesn’t
sharpen the edge, then he must use more strength;

2540
03:18:27,033 --> 03:18:28,633
but skill brings success.

2541
03:18:29,353 --> 03:18:34,873
If the snake bites before it is charmed,
then is there no profit for the charmer’s tongue.

2542
03:18:36,073 --> 03:18:42,053
The words of a wise man’s mouth are gracious;
but a fool is swallowed by his own lips.

2543
03:18:43,233 --> 03:18:48,913
The beginning of the words of his mouth is
foolishness; and the end of his talk is mischievous

2544
03:18:48,953 --> 03:18:49,853
madness.

2545
03:18:50,133 --> 03:18:52,173
A fool also multiplies words.

2546
03:18:53,313 --> 03:18:59,153
Man doesn’t know what will be; and that
which will be after him, who can tell him?

2547
03:18:59,893 --> 03:19:05,813
The labour of fools wearies every one of them;
for he doesn’t know how to go to the city.

2548
03:19:06,813 --> 03:19:12,393
Woe to you, land, when your king is
a child, and your princes eat in the morning!

2549
03:19:12,751 --> 03:19:19,251
Happy are you, land, when your king is the
son of nobles, and your princes eat in due

2550
03:19:19,291 --> 03:19:23,231
season, for strength, and not for
drunkenness!

2551
03:19:23,591 --> 03:19:29,511
By slothfulness the roof sinks in; and
through idleness of the hands the house leaks.

2552
03:19:30,831 --> 03:19:42,691
A feast is made for laughter, and wine
makes the life glad; and money is

2553
03:19:42,731 --> 03:19:43,031
the answer for all things.

2554
03:19:43,071 --> 03:19:46,211
Don’t curse the king, no, not in your
thoughts; and don’t curse the rich in your bedroom,

2555
03:19:47,131 --> 03:19:52,951
for a bird of the sky may carry your
voice, and that which has wings may tell the matter.

2556
03:19:53,371 --> 03:19:56,631
Ecclesiastes, chapter eleven.

2557
03:19:56,671 --> 03:20:01,171
Cast your bread on the waters; for you
shall find it after many days.

2558
03:20:02,231 --> 03:20:08,691
Give a portion to seven, yes, even to
eight; for you don’t know what evil will

2559
03:20:08,731 --> 03:20:09,631
be on the earth.

2560
03:20:10,211 --> 03:20:16,451
If the clouds are full of rain, they empty
themselves on the earth; and if a tree falls

2561
03:20:16,491 --> 03:20:22,771
towards the south, or towards the north, in
the place where the tree falls, there shall

2562
03:20:22,811 --> 03:20:23,711
it be.

2563
03:20:24,511 --> 03:20:29,911
He who observes the wind won’t sow; and he
who regards the clouds won’t reap.

2564
03:20:30,691 --> 03:20:35,891
As you don’t know what is the way of the
wind, nor how the bones grow in the womb of

2565
03:20:35,931 --> 03:20:41,751
her who is with child; even so you don’t
know the work of God who does all.

2566
03:20:42,751 --> 03:20:48,751
In the morning sow your seed, and in
the evening don’t withhold your hand; for you don’t

2567
03:20:48,791 --> 03:20:55,091
know which will prosper, whether this or that,
or whether they both will be equally good.

2568
03:20:56,131 --> 03:21:01,791
Truly the light is sweet, and it is a
pleasant thing for the eyes to see the sun.

2569
03:21:02,691 --> 03:21:09,531
Yes, if a man lives many years, let him
rejoice in them all; but let him remember

2570
03:21:09,571 --> 03:21:12,691
the days of darkness, for they shall be
many.

2571
03:21:13,751 --> 03:21:15,391
All that comes is vanity.

2572
03:21:16,551 --> 03:21:22,191
Rejoice, young man, in your youth, and let your
heart cheer you in the days of your youth,

2573
03:21:22,991 --> 03:21:28,731
and walk in the ways of your heart, and in
the sight of your eyes; but know that for

2574
03:21:28,771 --> 03:21:32,651
all these things God will bring you into
judgement.

2575
03:21:32,691 --> 03:21:39,171
Therefore remove sorrow from your heart,
and put away evil from your flesh; for

2576
03:21:39,211 --> 03:21:41,591
youth and the dawn of life are vanity.

2577
03:21:42,946 --> 03:21:45,626
Ecclesiastes, chapter twelve.

2578
03:21:45,666 --> 03:21:52,426
Remember also your Creator in the days of
your youth, before the evil days come, and

2579
03:21:52,466 --> 03:21:58,566
the years draw near, when you will say, “I
have no pleasure in them;” Before the sun,

2580
03:21:59,086 --> 03:22:04,926
the light, the moon, and the stars are
darkened, and the clouds return after the rain;

2581
03:22:05,706 --> 03:22:10,465
in the day when the keepers of the
house shall tremble, and the strong men shall bow

2582
03:22:10,506 --> 03:22:16,106
themselves, and the grinders cease because they are
few, and those who look out of the

2583
03:22:16,146 --> 03:22:21,266
windows are darkened, and the doors shall be
shut in the street; when the sound of the

2584
03:22:21,306 --> 03:22:27,126
grinding is low, and one shall rise up at
the voice of a bird, and all the daughters

2585
03:22:27,166 --> 03:22:33,985
of music shall be brought low; yes, they
shall be afraid of heights, and terrors

2586
03:22:34,026 --> 03:22:39,626
will be on the way; and the almond
tree shall blossom, and the grasshopper shall be a

2587
03:22:39,666 --> 03:22:46,626
burden, and desire shall fail; because man
goes to his everlasting home, and

2588
03:22:46,666 --> 03:22:52,426
the mourners go about the streets; before the
silver cord is severed, or the golden bowl

2589
03:22:52,466 --> 03:22:58,546
is broken, or the pitcher is broken at
the spring, or the wheel broken at the cistern,

2590
03:22:59,146 --> 03:23:04,766
and the dust returns to the earth as it
was, and the spirit returns to God who gave it.

2591
03:23:05,106 --> 03:23:07,226
“Vanity of vanities,” says the Preacher.

2592
03:23:08,126 --> 03:23:09,026
“All is vanity!”

2593
03:23:09,786 --> 03:23:14,606
Further, because the Preacher was wise, he
still taught the people knowledge.

2594
03:23:15,566 --> 03:23:20,306
Yes, he pondered, sought out, and set in
order many proverbs.

2595
03:23:21,306 --> 03:23:27,026
The Preacher sought to find out acceptable
words, and that which was written blamelessly,

2596
03:23:27,286 --> 03:23:28,186
words of truth.

2597
03:23:28,946 --> 03:23:35,006
The words of the wise are like goads;
and like nails well fastened are words from the

2598
03:23:35,046 --> 03:23:38,466
masters of assemblies, which are given
from one shepherd.

2599
03:23:39,586 --> 03:23:46,305
Furthermore, my son, be admonished: of
making many books there is no end; and

2600
03:23:46,346 --> 03:23:48,566
much study is a weariness of the flesh.

2601
03:23:49,686 --> 03:23:51,306
This is the end of the matter.

2602
03:23:51,866 --> 03:23:52,786
All has been heard.

2603
03:23:52,826 --> 03:23:58,706
Fear God and keep his commandments; for
this is the whole duty of man.

2604
03:23:59,113 --> 03:24:05,693
For God will bring every work into
judgement, with every hidden thing, whether it is

2605
03:24:05,733 --> 03:24:07,753
good, or whether it is evil.

